window.NOTES_DATA = {"en": {"verses": [{"n": "1", "text": "In beginning, God created the skies and the land.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRITICAL - Structure &amp; Interpretation</strong>", "body": "<p>Hebrew: <strong>בְּרֵאשִׁית בָּרָא אֱלֹהִים אֵת הַשָּׁמַיִם וְאֵת הָאָֽרֶץ</strong> (<em>Bereshit bara elohim et hashamayim ve'et ha'aretz</em>)</p><ul><li>Seven-word structure in Hebrew (symbolic number) lost in translation</li><li><strong>בְּרֵאשִׁית</strong> (<em>bereshit</em>) = \"in beginning\" (NO article—not \"in THE beginning\")</li><li>Grammatical structure permits TWO readings: (1) v.1 as independent sentence (traditional, followed here per Masoretic punctuation), or (2) v.1 as title/superscription with narrative beginning v.2. <strong>POSSIBLE</strong> that v.1 functions as chapter heading.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>KEY TERMS</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>אֵת</strong> (<em>et</em>) appears 2x—untranslatable direct object marker unique to Hebrew</li><li><strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em>) = specific divine creation term used distinctively for divine creative action; its precise scope (whether it implies creation from nothing or reshaping existing material) is debated (<strong>POSSIBLE</strong>); distinct from <strong>עָשָׂה</strong> (<em>asah</em> = make/form)</li><li><strong>שָׁמַיִם</strong> (<em>shamayim</em>) = physical sky (plural); NOT spiritual \"Heaven\"</li><li><strong>אֶרֶץ</strong> (<em>eretz</em>) = land/ground; NOT planet \"Earth\"</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "2", "text": "And the land was chaos and void, and darkness <em>was</em> over the face of the deep, and wind/spirit of God <em>was</em> hovering over the face of the waters.", "notes": [{"type": "theological", "title": "<strong>AMBIGUITY PRESERVED</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>תֹהוּ וָבֹהוּ</strong> (<em>tohu vavohu</em>) = rare phrase (appears only 3x in Bible); exact meaning <strong>UNCERTAIN</strong>; associated with destruction/desolation. \"Chaos and void\" is <strong>POSSIBLE</strong> translation. Avoid elaborate cosmological speculation.</li><li><strong>רוּחַ אֱלֹהִים</strong> (<em>ruach elohim</em>) = wind/spirit/breath of God—ALL THREE meanings present; grammatically feminine in Hebrew</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>KEY TERMS</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>תְהוֹם</strong> (<em>tehom</em>) = the deep/massive body of water; <strong>PROBABLE</strong> translation; avoid \"cosmic ocean\" (false precision)</li><li><strong>מְרַחֶפֶת</strong> (<em>merachefet</em>) = present participle (ongoing action)—NOT simple past \"hovered\"; possibly \"brooding\" or \"covering\"</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "3", "text": "And God said, \"Shall be light,\" and light was.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>JUSSIVE &amp; CONVERTING VAV</strong> (Explained here; not repeated in later verses)", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יְהִי</strong> (<em>yehi</em>) = future/jussive form used as divine command—literally \"shall be\" rather than imperative \"let there be\"</li><li><strong>Converting-vav (ו)</strong> on <strong>וַיְהִי</strong> (<em>vayehi</em>) changes future \"shall be\" → past narrative \"and was\"—unique biblical Hebrew feature that propels narrative forward. This pattern continues throughout Genesis 1.</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "4", "text": "And God saw the light, that good, and God separated between the light and between the darkness.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>COMPRESSED EVALUATION</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Hebrew <strong>כִּי־טוֹב</strong> (<em>ki-tov</em>) = \"that good\" without explicit \"it was\"—Transparent Edition preserves Hebrew compression; Reader Edition would expand to \"that it was good\"</li><li>\"Between...and between\" (<strong>בֵּין...וּבֵין</strong>) = Hebrew repetitive pattern preserved; continues in vv.6, 7, 14, 18</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "5", "text": "And God called to the light \"Day,\" and to the darkness he called \"Night.\" And was evening, and was morning, one day.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRITICAL - Day ONE, Not FIRST</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Hebrew <strong>יוֹם אֶחָד</strong> (<em>yom echad</em>) = \"day ONE\" (cardinal number)—NOT ordinal <strong>רִאשׁוֹן</strong> (<em>rishon</em> = \"first\"). Days 2-6 use ordinals (second, third, fourth, fifth, sixth). <strong>Day 1 treated differently linguistically—this is significant.</strong></li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>DAY CLOSURE FORMULA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>\"And was evening, and was morning, [X] day\" = LOCKED formula; repeats exactly in vv.8, 13, 19, 23, 31</li><li>Evening-morning order reflects Hebrew day beginning at sunset</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "6", "text": "And God said, \"Shall be <em>a</em> raqia (expanse) within the waters, and <em>it</em> shall be a separator between waters to waters.\"", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRITICAL - RAQIA INTRODUCTION</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Hebrew <strong>רָקִיעַ</strong> (<em>raqia</em>) from root <strong>ר-ק-ע</strong> = \"to hammer/beat\"—describes hammered or beaten-out structure</li><li><strong>TRANSLITERATED</strong> throughout Genesis 1 to prevent false cosmological precision</li><li>Verse 8 will identify <strong>raqia = shamayim (sky)</strong></li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>STRUCTURE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בְּתוֹךְ</strong> (<em>betoch</em>) = \"within/inside\" the waters (the raqia forms inside the water mass)—not \"amid/among\"</li><li><strong>מַבְדִּיל</strong> (<em>mavdil</em>) = Hiphil participle used substantivally: \"a separator/divider\"—not the finite \"separates\" or the infinitive \"to separate\"</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "7", "text": "And God made the raqia, and he separated between the waters which <em>were</em> under the raqia and between the waters which <em>were</em> above the raqia. And it was so.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>VERB SHIFT</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = created, v.1) vs. <strong>עָשָׂה</strong> (<em>asah</em> = made, v.7)—both used for divine action; <strong>POSSIBLE</strong> distinction: <em>bara</em> is used distinctively for divine creative action; its precise scope (whether it implies creation from nothing or reshaping existing material) is debated</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>FORMULA INTRODUCED</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>\"And it was so\" (<strong>וַיְהִי־כֵן</strong>) appears for first time; repeats in vv.9, 11, 15, 24, 30</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "8", "text": "And God called to the raqia \"Sky.\" And was evening, and was morning, second day.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRITICAL - RAQIA = SKY IDENTIFICATION</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>God explicitly identifies <strong>raqia = shamayim (sky)</strong>—the text equates raqia with the visible sky/expanse above. The semantic range of raqia (from root \"to hammer/beat out\") remains debated; ancient interpreters understood it variously as a solid vault, an atmospheric expanse, or a boundary layer. The naming here grounds the term in the sky domain without resolving those questions.</li><li>Subsequent verses using \"raqia\" (vv.14-20) maintain this identification</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>DAY 2 ORDINAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יוֹם שֵׁנִי</strong> (<em>yom sheni</em>) = \"second day\" (ordinal)—unlike Day 1's cardinal \"one\"</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "9", "text": "And God said, \"Shall be gathered the waters from under the sky to one place, and shall be seen the dry ground.\" And it was so.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>PASSIVE VOICE PRESERVED</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יִקָּווּ</strong> (<em>yikavu</em>) = \"shall be gathered\" (passive); <strong>תֵרָאֶה</strong> (<em>teira'eh</em>) = \"shall be seen\" (passive)—not active commands to waters, but passive divine causation</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>WORD ROOT</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יִקָּווּ</strong> from root <strong>ק-ו-ה</strong> (gather/collect)—related to <strong>מִקְוֵה</strong> (<em>miqveh</em> = ritual bath, water-gathering)</li><li>Singular \"place\" for land (connected landmass) anticipates plural \"seas\" v.10</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "10", "text": "And God called to the dry ground \"Land,\" and to the gathering of the waters he called \"Seas.\" And God saw that good.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>SINGULAR vs. PLURAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>אֶרֶץ</strong> (<em>eretz</em>) = land (SINGULAR connected landmass); <strong>יַמִּים</strong> (<em>yamim</em>) = seas (PLURAL separated bodies of water)</li><li>Hebrew distinguishes one land from multiple seas (Mediterranean + Red Sea separated in ancient geography)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "11", "text": "And God said, \"Shall grass the land grass, herbs seeding seed, fruit trees making fruit to its kind, which its seed <em>is</em> in it, upon the land.\" And it was so.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>RARE VERB - \"TO GRASS\"</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>תַּדְשֵׁא</strong> (<em>tadsheh</em>) = verb created from noun <strong>דֶּשֶׁא</strong> (grass)—similar to English \"to grass\" (produce grass). YES, \"shall grass\" sounds odd—<strong>intentional preservation of Hebrew poetic style.</strong></li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>ROOT DOUBLING PATTERNS</strong> (Hebrew poetic device)", "body": "<ul><li><strong>מַזְרִיעַ זֶרַע</strong> (<em>mazria zera</em>) = \"seeding seed\"; <strong>עֹשֶׂה פְרִי</strong> (<em>oseh pri</em>) = \"making fruit\"</li><li>Shows internal production/generation—<strong>preserved despite awkwardness</strong></li><li><strong>דֶּשֶׁא עֵשֶׂב</strong> (<em>deshe esev</em>) = \"grass, herbs\" (synonym pairing for stylistic effect)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>REPRODUCTION PATTERN</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>לְמִינוֹ</strong> (<em>lemino</em>) = \"to its kind/type\"—describes reproduction pattern</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "12", "text": "And the land brought out grass, herbs seeding seed to its kind, and trees making fruit which its seed <em>is</em> in it, to its kind. And God saw that good.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>COMMAND → FULFILLMENT PATTERN</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>v.11 command → v.12 fulfillment with nearly identical wording—shows exact compliance</li><li>Root doubling maintained: \"seeding seed,\" \"making fruit\"</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "13", "text": "And was evening, and was morning, third day.", "notes": []}, {"n": "14", "text": "And God said, \"Shall be lights in the raqia, to separate between the day and between the night, and they shall be for signs and for appointed times and for days and years.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>LUMINARIES INTRODUCED</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>מְאֹרֹת</strong> (<em>me'orot</em>) = lights/luminaries/light-bearers from root <strong>א-ו-ר</strong> (light)—plural but specific referents unnamed until v.16</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>RAQIA REFERENCE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>After v.8 identified raqia = sky, this verse places lights \"in the raqia\"</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>APPOINTED TIMES</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>מוֹעֲדִים</strong> (<em>mo'adim</em>) = appointed times/seasons/festivals—can mean natural seasons OR sacred calendar events; meaning range preserved</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "15", "text": "And they shall be for lights in the raqia, to give light upon the land.\" And it was so.", "notes": []}, {"n": "16", "text": "And God made the two great lights: the greater light for dominion of the day, and the lesser light for dominion of the night, and the stars.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRITICAL - UNNAMED LUMINARIES</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Sun and moon <strong>LEFT UNNAMED</strong>—described only as \"greater light\" and \"lesser light\"</li><li>It has been noted that Genesis 1:16 avoids the common Hebrew words for sun (<em>shemesh</em>) and moon (<em>yareach</em>), which are also names of deities in the ancient Near East. Whether this avoidance is deliberate is debated (<strong>POSSIBLE</strong>).</li><li>Transparent Edition resists identifying them by name</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>DOMINION = TEMPORAL RULE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>מֶמְשֶׁלֶת</strong> (<em>memsheleth</em>) = dominion/rule over <strong>time periods</strong>—NOT territorial rule</li><li>\"And the stars\" added almost as syntactic afterthought—structure emphasizes the two lights</li><li><strong>עָשָׂה</strong> (<em>asah</em> = made) used, NOT <strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = created)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "17", "text": "And God set them in the raqia, to give light upon the land.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>PLACEMENT</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Lights placed <strong>IN</strong> the raqia—contrast: birds fly <strong>OVER</strong> the raqia (v.20)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "18", "text": "And to rule in the day and in the night, and to separate between the light and between the darkness. And God saw that good.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>PURPOSE INFINITIVES</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>\"To rule...and to separate\"—parallel functions of the lights</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "19", "text": "And was evening, and was morning, fourth day.", "notes": []}, {"n": "20", "text": "And God said, \"Shall swarm the waters <em>with</em> swarms of living beings, and birds shall fly over the land, over the face of the raqia.\"", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRITICAL - LIVING BEINGS INTRODUCED</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה</strong> (<em>nefesh chayah</em>) = living being/beings—literally \"living breath/throat/soul\"; <strong>NOT \"soul\" in later philosophical sense</strong></li><li>Added to glossary; used in vv.21, 24, 30</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>ROOT DOUBLING</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>שֶׁרֶץ</strong> (<em>sherets</em> = swarms) from <strong>יִשְׁרְצוּ</strong> (<em>yishretzu</em> = shall swarm)</li><li><strong>יְעוֹפֵף</strong> (<em>ye'ofef</em>) = doubled/intensive form \"flying-fly\"</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>SPATIAL RELATIONSHIP</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Birds fly <strong>OVER the face of</strong> the raqia—NOT <strong>IN</strong> it (contrast: lights <strong>IN</strong> raqia)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "21", "text": "And God created the great sea creatures, and every living being, the moving <em>ones</em> which the waters swarmed, to their kinds, and every winged bird to its kind. And God saw that good.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRITICAL - CREATED, NOT MADE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = created) returns for first time since v.1—used for living beings, NOT for lights or plants; suggests significance distinction</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>SEA CREATURES</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>תַּנִּינִים</strong> (<em>taninim</em>) = great sea creatures/large aquatic animals—avoiding \"sea monsters\" or \"dragons\" (mythological overlay)</li><li><strong>לְמִינֵהֶם/לְמִינֵהוּ</strong> (<em>leminehem/leminehu</em>) = \"to their kinds\"—reproduction pattern as in v.11</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "22", "text": "And God blessed them, saying, \"Be fruitful and multiply, and fill the waters in the seas, and <em>let</em> the birds multiply in the land.\"", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>FIRST BLESSING FORMULA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>וַיְבָרֶךְ</strong> (<em>vayvarekh</em>) = \"and he blessed\" (first occurrence)—will recur: v.28 (humans), Genesis 2:3 (seventh day)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>TRIPLE IMPERATIVE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>פְּרוּ</strong> (<em>peru</em>) = be fruitful; <strong>וּרְבוּ</strong> (<em>urvu</em>) = multiply; <strong>וּמִלְאוּ</strong> (<em>umil'u</em>) = fill</li><li><strong>לֵאמֹר</strong> (<em>lemor</em> = \"saying\") introduces direct divine speech to creatures—unusual narrative feature</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "23", "text": "And was evening, and was morning, fifth day.", "notes": []}, {"n": "24", "text": "And God said, \"Shall bring forth the land living beings to their kind: livestock and creeping things and living things of <em>the</em> land, to their kind.\" And it was so.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>NEFESH CHAYAH - Land Animals</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה</strong> now applied to land animals (previously water creatures, vv.20-21)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>THREE CATEGORIES</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בְּהֵמָה</strong> (<em>behemah</em>) = livestock/cattle; <strong>רֶמֶשׂ</strong> (<em>remes</em>) = creeping things; <strong>חַיְתוֹ־אֶרֶץ</strong> (<em>chayeto-eretz</em>) = living things of land/wild animals</li><li>Pattern parallels Day 3 vegetation: land brings forth on divine command</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "25", "text": "And God made the living things of the land to their kind, and the livestock to their kind, and every creeping thing of the ground to its kind. And God saw that good.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>GROUND vs. LAND</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>אֲדָמָה</strong> (<em>adamah</em>) = ground/soil (FIRST occurrence)—distinct from <strong>אֶרֶץ</strong> (<em>eretz</em> = land)</li><li><strong>עָשָׂה</strong> (<em>asah</em> = made), NOT <strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = created)</li><li>Command (v.24) → fulfillment (v.25) pattern as in Days 3-4</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "26", "text": "And God said, \"Let us make <em>a</em> human in our image, according to our likeness, and let them have dominion over <em>the</em> fish of the sea and over <em>the</em> birds of the sky and over the livestock and over all the land and over every creeping thing <em>that</em> creeps upon the land.\"", "notes": [{"type": "theological", "title": "<strong>CRITICAL - PLURAL DIVINE SPEECH</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>First person <strong>PLURAL</strong>: \"let <strong>us</strong> make...in <strong>our</strong> image...our likeness\"</li><li><strong>POSSIBLE</strong> interpretations: (1) royal plural, (2) divine council, (3) literary plural</li><li>Note marks <strong>UNCERTAINTY</strong>—does NOT impose Trinity interpretation</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>HUMAN = GENERIC</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>אָדָם</strong> (<em>adam</em>) WITHOUT article = generic human/humanity—NOT yet proper name \"Adam\"</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>IMAGE &amp; LIKENESS</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>צֶלֶם</strong> (<em>tselem</em>) = image; <strong>דְּמוּת</strong> (<em>demut</em>) = likeness</li><li>Both = representation/resemblance; paired for emphasis, NOT identical meaning</li><li><strong>Cross-reference:</strong> The pair re-appears at <strong>Gen 5:3</strong> — Adam begets Seth \"in his likeness, according to his image,\" inverting the divine-human order into human-human descent. For fuller discussion, see companion Section A12b.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>DOMINION = FUNCTIONAL RULE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>רָדָה</strong> (<em>radah</em>) = have dominion/rule/govern—functional authority, <strong>NOT ownership</strong></li><li>Verb shifts: \"make A human\" (singular) → \"let THEM have dominion\" (plural)</li><li><strong>הָרֶמֶשׂ הָֽרֹמֵשׂ</strong> (<em>haremes haromes</em>) = \"creeping thing that creeps\" (root doubling)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "27", "text": "And God created the human in his image; in <em>the</em> image of God he created him; male and female he created them.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRITICAL - TRIPLE CREATION EMPHASIS</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = created) used <strong>THREE TIMES</strong>—<strong>ONLY occurrence</strong> of triple verb repetition in one verse; shows maximum significance/emphasis</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>POETIC STRUCTURE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Three parallel clauses with <strong>bara</strong> anchoring each—elevated literary style</li><li>Singular/plural shift: \"the human...him\" (SINGULAR) → \"male and female...them\" (PLURAL)—collective humanity becomes differentiated</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>BIOLOGICAL DIFFERENTIATION</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>זָכָר וּנְקֵבָה</strong> (<em>zakhar unqevah</em>) = male and female—grammatical terms for biological sex, NOT gendered cultural roles</li><li><strong>הָאָדָם</strong> (<em>ha'adam</em>) = \"THE human\" (with article) vs. v.26 <strong>אָדָם</strong> (without article)—<strong>POSSIBLE</strong> emphasis</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "28", "text": "And God blessed them, and God said to them, \"Be fruitful and multiply, and fill the land and subdue it, and have dominion over <em>the</em> fish of the sea and over <em>the</em> birds of the sky and over every living thing <em>that</em> moves upon the land.\"", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>BLESSING FORMULA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>As v.22 (sea creatures/birds), but expanded for humans with additional commands</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>FIVE IMPERATIVES</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Be fruitful, multiply, fill, <strong>subdue</strong>, <strong>have dominion</strong></li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>SUBDUE = CULTIVATION</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>כָּבַשׁ</strong> (<em>kabash</em>) = subdue/bring under cultivation—agricultural term (appears ONLY here in Genesis 1); <strong>NOT license for exploitation or violence</strong></li><li><strong>רָדָה</strong> (<em>radah</em>) now as imperative—functional rule over animals, NOT absolute ownership</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>CROSS-REFERENCE: POST-FLOOD REPETITION</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>The \"be fruitful and multiply and fill the land\" command re-appears verbatim at <strong>Gen 9:1</strong> — the creation-mandate renewed after the flood. The dominion language in 9:2 shifts tone (animals <em>fear</em> humans) and diet permission expands (9:3, meat permitted). For fuller discussion, see companion Section G5b.</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "29", "text": "And God said, \"See, I have given to you every herb seeding seed which <em>is</em> upon <em>the</em> face of all the land, and every tree in which <em>is</em> fruit of <em>a</em> tree seeding seed; to you it shall be for food.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>ATTENTION PARTICLE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>הִנֵּה</strong> (<em>hineh</em>) = \"see/behold\"—signals important announcement</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>ROOT DOUBLING</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>זֹרֵעַ זֶרַע</strong> (<em>zorea zera</em>) = \"seeding seed\"—pattern from vv.11-12</li></ul>"}, {"type": "theological", "title": "<strong>ORIGINAL DIET</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Vegetation ONLY for humans—NO animal consumption permitted yet (contrast Genesis 9:3 post-flood permission)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "30", "text": "And to every living thing of the land and to every bird of the sky and to everything creeping upon the land, in which <em>is a</em> living being, every green herb <em>shall be</em> for food.\" And it was so.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>NEFESH CHAYAH = Qualifier</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה</strong> distinguishes animals with breath/life from plants</li></ul>"}, {"type": "theological", "title": "<strong>UNIVERSAL VEGETARIAN DIET</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>ALL living beings eat only plants initially—animals also vegetarian in original creation</li><li><strong>יֶרֶק עֵשֶׂב</strong> (<em>yereq esev</em>) = green herb/fresh vegetation</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "31", "text": "And God saw all that he had made, and see, <em>it was</em> very good. And was evening, and was morning, the sixth day.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRITICAL - EVALUATION SHIFT: VERY GOOD</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>טוֹב מְאֹד</strong> (<em>tov me'od</em>) = \"VERY good\" vs. simple <strong>טוֹב</strong> (<em>tov</em> = \"good\") in ALL previous days</li><li><strong>ONLY occurrence</strong> of \"very good\" in creation account—shows comprehensive positive evaluation after human creation</li><li><strong>THIS IS NOT STYLISTIC VARIATION—IT'S THEOLOGICAL SIGNIFICANCE</strong></li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>HINEH = Attention</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>הִנֵּה</strong> (<em>hineh</em> = \"see/behold\") appears with evaluation—draws attention to comprehensive goodness</li><li>\"All that he had made\"—entire creation reviewed</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRITICAL - ARTICLE ON \"THE SIXTH DAY\"</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יוֹם הַשִּׁשִּׁי</strong> (<em>yom hashishi</em>) = \"THE sixth day\" with definite article <strong>ה</strong></li><li><strong>UNIQUE among all six days</strong> (Days 1-5 have NO article)</li><li><strong>POSSIBLE</strong> significance: completion emphasis, human creation importance, or preparation for Sabbath (Genesis 2:1-3)</li><li><strong>Many translations miss this distinction</strong></li></ul>"}]}], "glossary": {"headers": ["Hebrew", "English", "Notes"], "rows": [["אֱלֹהִים", "God", "Plural form, singular verb"], ["אֶרֶץ", "land", "\"Ground\" only when clearly soil"], ["אֲדָמָה", "ground, soil", "Distinct from <em>eretz</em>"], ["שָׁמַיִם", "sky, skies", "NOT \"Heaven\""], ["רָקִיעַ", "raqia", "Transliterated; v.8 = sky"], ["מַיִם", "waters <em>(default)</em> / water <em>(contextual)</em>", "Default plural where context is plural-meaningful (separated bodies, gathered waters). Contextual singular \"water\" permitted where forcing \"waters\" would import KJV register; test per Rule 3. All shifts logged."], ["רוּחַ", "wind/spirit", "May add \"breath\" in notes"], ["תְהוֹם", "the deep", "Avoid speculation"], ["תֹהוּ וָבֹהוּ", "chaos and void", "Rare; uncertain meaning"], ["נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה", "living being(s)", "NOT \"soul\" philosophically"], ["בָּרָא", "created", "Divine creation; v.1, 21, 27"], ["עָשָׂה", "made", "Formation; v.7, 16, 25"], ["צֶלֶם", "image", "Paired with <em>demut</em>"], ["דְּמוּת", "likeness", "Paired with <em>tselem</em>"], ["אָדָם", "human", "Generic; \"Adam\" when proper"], ["רָדָה", "have dominion", "Functional rule"], ["כָּבַשׁ", "subdue", "Agricultural term"]]}, "supplementary": [{"title": "FORMULA TRACKING", "body": "<p><strong>Locked Formulas (Multiple Occurrences):</strong></p><ul><li>\"And God said...\" (10x)</li><li>\"And it was so\" (6x — vv.7, 9, 11, 15, 24, 30)</li><li>\"And God saw that good\" (6x) + \"very good\" (1x at v.31)</li><li>\"And was evening, and was morning, [X] day\" (6x)</li><li>\"And God blessed them\" (2x: vv.22, 28)</li><li>\"Be fruitful and multiply\" (2x: vv.22, 28)</li></ul><p><strong>Significant Variations:</strong></p><ul><li>v.5: \"one day\" (cardinal) vs. vv.8,13,19,23,31 (ordinals)</li><li>v.31: \"very good\" (NOT simple \"good\") + \"THE sixth day\" (article unique)</li></ul>"}, {"title": "ROOT DOUBLING PATTERNS", "body": "<p>Hebrew poetic device showing internal generation:</p><ul><li>v.11-12: \"seeding seed\" (<strong>מַזְרִיעַ זֶרַע</strong>), \"making fruit\" (<strong>עֹשֶׂה פְרִי</strong>)</li><li>v.20: \"swarms\" from \"shall swarm\"</li><li>v.26: \"creeping thing that creeps\" (<strong>הָרֶמֶשׂ הָֽרֹמֵשׂ</strong>)</li><li>v.29: \"seeding seed\" (<strong>זֹרֵעַ זֶרַע</strong>)</li></ul><p><strong>Preserved despite sounding awkward—intentional Hebrew poetic style.</strong></p>"}, {"title": "VERB SHIFTS - CREATED vs. MADE", "body": "<table class=\"cmp\"><thead><tr><th>Verse</th><th>Action</th><th>Verb</th><th>Hebrew</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>v.1</td><td>Skies and land</td><td><strong>created</strong></td><td><em>bara</em> בָּרָא</td></tr><tr><td>v.7</td><td>Raqia</td><td>made</td><td><em>asah</em> עָשָׂה</td></tr><tr><td>v.16</td><td>Lights</td><td>made</td><td><em>asah</em></td></tr><tr><td>v.21</td><td>Sea creatures &amp; living beings</td><td><strong>created</strong></td><td><em>bara</em></td></tr><tr><td>v.25</td><td>Land animals</td><td>made</td><td><em>asah</em></td></tr><tr><td>v.27</td><td>Human (3x emphasis)</td><td><strong>created</strong></td><td><em>bara</em></td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Pattern:</strong> <em>Bara</em> (created) for initial creation, living beings, humans. <em>Asah</em> (made) for raqia, lights, land animals. <strong>POSSIBLE</strong> distinction: <em>bara</em> is used distinctively for divine creative action; its precise scope (whether it implies creation from nothing or reshaping existing material) is debated.</p><p><strong>END OF GENESIS 1 - THE TRANSPARENT TRANSLATION (ENGLISH)</strong></p>"}]}, "pt-br": {"verses": [{"n": "1", "text": "Em princípio, Deus criou os céus e a terra.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - Estrutura e Interpretação</strong>", "body": "<p>Hebraico: <strong>בְּרֵאשִׁית בָּרָא אֱלֹהִים אֵת הַשָּׁמַיִם וְאֵת הָאָֽרֶץ</strong> (<em>Bereshit bara elohim et hashamayim ve'et ha'aretz</em>)</p><ul><li>Estrutura de sete palavras em hebraico (número simbólico) perdida na tradução</li><li><strong>בְּרֵאשִׁית</strong> (<em>bereshit</em>) = \"em princípio\" (SEM artigo—não \"no princípio\")</li><li>Estrutura gramatical permite DUAS leituras: (1) v.1 como sentença independente (tradicional, seguida aqui conforme pontuação massorética), ou (2) v.1 como título/sobrescrição com narrativa começando v.2. <strong>POSSÍVEL</strong> que v.1 funcione como cabeçalho do capítulo.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>TERMOS-CHAVE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>אֵת</strong> (<em>et</em>) aparece 2x—marcador de objeto direto intraduzível, único ao hebraico</li><li><strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em>) = usado distintivamente para a ação criativa divina; seu escopo preciso (se implica criação do nada ou remodelação de material existente) é debatido (POSSÍVEL); distinto de <strong>עָשָׂה</strong> (<em>asah</em> = fazer/formar)</li><li><strong>שָׁמַיִם</strong> (<em>shamayim</em>) = céu físico (plural); NÃO \"Céu\" espiritual</li><li><strong>אֶרֶץ</strong> (<em>eretz</em>) = terra/solo; NÃO planeta \"Terra\"</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "2", "text": "E a terra estava caos e vazio, e trevas sobre a face do abismo, e vento/espírito de Deus pairando sobre a face das águas.", "notes": [{"type": "theological", "title": "<strong>AMBIGUIDADE PRESERVADA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>תֹהוּ וָבֹהוּ</strong> (<em>tohu vavohu</em>) = frase rara (aparece apenas 3x na Bíblia); significado exato <strong>INCERTO</strong>; associada com destruição/desolação. \"Caos e vazio\" é tradução <strong>POSSÍVEL</strong>. Evitar especulação cosmológica elaborada.</li><li><strong>רוּחַ אֱלֹהִים</strong> (<em>ruach elohim</em>) = vento/espírito/sopro de Deus—TODOS TRÊS significados presentes; gramaticalmente feminino em hebraico</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>TERMOS-CHAVE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>תְהוֹם</strong> (<em>tehom</em>) = o abismo/corpo massivo de água; tradução <strong>PROVÁVEL</strong>; evitar \"oceano cósmico\" (falsa precisão)</li><li><strong>מְרַחֶפֶת</strong> (<em>merachefet</em>) = particípio presente (ação contínua)—NÃO passado simples \"pairou\"; possivelmente \"cobrindo\" ou \"chocando\"</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "3", "text": "E Deus disse: \"Haja luz,\" e luz foi.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>JUSSIVO &amp; VAV CONVERSIVO</strong> (Explicado aqui; não repetido em versículos posteriores)", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יְהִי</strong> (<em>yehi</em>) = forma futura/jussiva usada como comando divino—literalmente \"será\" em vez de imperativo</li><li>Subjuntivo português \"haja\" captura perfeitamente a função jussiva hebraica</li><li><strong>Vav conversivo (ו)</strong> em <strong>וַיְהִי</strong> (<em>vayehi</em>) muda futuro \"será\" → narrativa passada \"e foi\"—característica única do hebraico bíblico que impulsiona a narrativa. Este padrão continua em Gênesis 1.</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "4", "text": "E Deus viu a luz, que bom, e Deus separou entre a luz e entre as trevas.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>AVALIAÇÃO COMPRIMIDA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Hebraico <strong>כִּי־טוֹב</strong> (<em>ki-tov</em>) = \"que bom\" sem explícito \"era\"—Edição Transparente preserva compressão hebraica; Edição do Leitor expandiria para \"que era bom\"</li><li>\"Entre...e entre\" (<strong>בֵּין...וּבֵין</strong>) = padrão repetitivo hebraico preservado; continua em vv.6, 7, 14, 18</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "5", "text": "E Deus chamou à luz \"Dia,\" e às trevas chamou \"Noite.\" E foi tarde, e foi manhã, um dia.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - Dia UM, Não PRIMEIRO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Hebraico <strong>יוֹם אֶחָד</strong> (<em>yom echad</em>) = \"dia UM\" (número cardinal)—NÃO ordinal <strong>רִאשׁוֹן</strong> (<em>rishon</em> = \"primeiro\"). Dias 2-6 usam ordinais (segundo, terceiro, quarto, quinto, sexto). <strong>Dia 1 tratado linguisticamente diferente—isto é significativo.</strong></li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>FÓRMULA DE FECHAMENTO DO DIA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>\"E foi tarde, e foi manhã, [X] dia\" = fórmula TRAVADA; repete exatamente em vv.8, 13, 19, 23, 31</li><li>Ordem tarde-manhã reflete dia hebraico começando ao pôr do sol</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "6", "text": "E Deus disse: \"Haja raqia (expansão) dentro das águas, e seja um separador entre águas e águas.\"", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - INTRODUÇÃO DO RAQIA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Hebraico <strong>רָקִיעַ</strong> (<em>raqia</em>) da raiz <strong>ר-ק-ע</strong> = \"martelar/bater\"—descreve estrutura martelada ou batida</li><li><strong>TRANSLITERADO</strong> em todo Gênesis 1 para prevenir falsa precisão cosmológica</li><li>Versículo 8 identificará <strong>raqia = shamayim (céu)</strong></li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>ESTRUTURA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בְּתוֹךְ</strong> (<em>betoch</em>) = \"dentro\" das águas (o raqia forma-se dentro da massa de água)—não \"no meio de/entre\"</li><li><strong>מַבְדִּיל</strong> (<em>mavdil</em>) = particípio Hifil usado substantivamente: \"um separador/divisor\"—não o finito \"separa\" nem o infinitivo \"separar\"</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "7", "text": "E Deus fez o raqia, e separou entre as águas que debaixo do raqia e entre as águas que acima do raqia. E foi assim.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>MUDANÇA DE VERBO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = criou, v.1) vs. <strong>עָשָׂה</strong> (<em>asah</em> = fez, v.7)—ambos usados para ação divina; distinção <strong>POSSÍVEL</strong>: o escopo preciso de <em>bara</em> (se implica criação do nada ou remodelação de material existente) é debatido</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>FÓRMULA INTRODUZIDA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>\"E foi assim\" (<strong>וַיְהִי־כֵן</strong>) aparece pela primeira vez; repete em vv.9, 11, 15, 24, 30</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "8", "text": "E Deus chamou ao raqia \"Céu.\" E foi tarde, e foi manhã, segundo dia.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - RAQIA = IDENTIFICAÇÃO COM CÉU</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Deus explicitamente identifica <strong>raqia = shamayim (céu)</strong>—o texto confirma que <em>raqia</em> refere-se ao céu/expansão visível acima. O alcance semântico de <em>raqia</em> (da raiz \"martelar/bater\") permanece debatido; intérpretes antigos o entenderam variadamente como abóbada sólida, expansão atmosférica ou camada-limite. A nomeação aqui ancora o termo no domínio celeste sem resolver essas questões.</li><li>Versículos subsequentes usando \"raqia\" (vv.14-20) mantêm esta identificação</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>DIA 2 ORDINAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יוֹם שֵׁנִי</strong> (<em>yom sheni</em>) = \"segundo dia\" (ordinal)—diferente do cardinal \"um\" do Dia 1</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "9", "text": "E Deus disse: \"Sejam ajuntadas as águas de debaixo do céu a um lugar, e seja vista a terra seca.\" E foi assim.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>VOZ PASSIVA PRESERVADA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יִקָּווּ</strong> (<em>yikavu</em>) = \"sejam ajuntadas\" (passiva); <strong>תֵרָאֶה</strong> (<em>teira'eh</em>) = \"seja vista\" (passiva)—não comandos ativos às águas, mas causação divina passiva</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>RAIZ DA PALAVRA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יִקָּווּ</strong> da raiz <strong>ק-ו-ה</strong> (ajuntar/coletar)—relacionado a <strong>מִקְוֵה</strong> (<em>miqveh</em> = banho ritual, ajuntamento de água)</li><li>\"Lugar\" singular para terra (massa continental conectada) antecipa \"mares\" plural v.10</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "10", "text": "E Deus chamou à terra seca \"Terra,\" e ao ajuntamento das águas chamou \"Mares.\" E Deus viu que bom.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>SINGULAR vs. PLURAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>אֶרֶץ</strong> (<em>eretz</em>) = terra (SINGULAR massa continental conectada); <strong>יַמִּים</strong> (<em>yamim</em>) = mares (PLURAL corpos de água separados)</li><li>Hebraico distingue uma terra de múltiplos mares (Mediterrâneo + Mar Vermelho separados na geografia antiga)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "11", "text": "E Deus disse: \"Produza a terra relva, ervas semeando semente, árvores frutíferas fazendo fruto segundo a sua espécie, cuja semente nela, sobre a terra.\" E foi assim.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>VERBO RARO - \"PRODUZIR RELVA\"</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>תַּדְשֵׁא</strong> (<em>tadsheh</em>) = verbo criado do substantivo <strong>דֶּשֶׁא</strong> (relva)—similar a \"produzir relva\". Português mantém naturalidade melhor que inglês \"shall grass\".</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>PADRÕES DE DUPLICAÇÃO DE RAIZ</strong> (dispositivo poético hebraico)", "body": "<ul><li><strong>מַזְרִיעַ זֶרַע</strong> (<em>mazria zera</em>) = \"semeando semente\"; <strong>עֹשֶׂה פְרִי</strong> (<em>oseh pri</em>) = \"fazendo fruto\"</li><li>Mostra produção/geração interna—<strong>preservado apesar da repetição</strong></li><li><strong>דֶּשֶׁא עֵשֶׂב</strong> (<em>deshe esev</em>) = \"relva, ervas\" (pareamento de sinônimos para efeito estilístico)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>PADRÃO DE REPRODUÇÃO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>לְמִינוֹ</strong> (<em>lemino</em>) = \"segundo a sua espécie\"—descreve padrão reprodutivo</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "12", "text": "E a terra produziu relva, ervas semeando semente segundo a sua espécie, e árvores fazendo fruto cuja semente nela, segundo a sua espécie. E Deus viu que bom.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>PADRÃO COMANDO → CUMPRIMENTO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>v.11 comando → v.12 cumprimento com redação quase idêntica—mostra conformidade exata</li><li>Duplicação de raiz mantida: \"semeando semente,\" \"fazendo fruto\"</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "13", "text": "E foi tarde, e foi manhã, terceiro dia.", "notes": []}, {"n": "14", "text": "E Deus disse: \"Haja luminares no raqia, para separar entre o dia e entre a noite, e sejam para sinais e para tempos determinados e para dias e anos.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>LUMINARES INTRODUZIDOS</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>מְאֹרֹת</strong> (<em>me'orot</em>) = luminares/portadores de luz da raiz <strong>א-ו-ר</strong> (luz)—plural mas referentes específicos não nomeados até v.16</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>REFERÊNCIA AO RAQIA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Após v.8 identificar raqia = céu, este versículo coloca luzes \"no raqia\"</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>TEMPOS DETERMINADOS</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>מוֹעֲדִים</strong> (<em>mo'adim</em>) = tempos determinados/estações/festivais—pode significar estações naturais OU eventos de calendário sagrado; amplitude de significado preservada</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "15", "text": "E sejam para luminares no raqia, para alumiar sobre a terra.\" E foi assim.", "notes": []}, {"n": "16", "text": "E Deus fez os dois grandes luminares: o luminar maior para domínio do dia, e o luminar menor para domínio da noite, e as estrelas.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - LUMINARES NÃO NOMEADOS</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Sol e lua <strong>DEIXADOS SEM NOME</strong>—descritos apenas como \"luminar maior\" e \"luminar menor\"</li><li>Contexto do Oriente Próximo Antigo: evitando nomes de divindades usados em culturas circundantes</li><li>Edição Transparente resiste identificá-los por nome</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>DOMÍNIO = GOVERNO TEMPORAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>מֶמְשֶׁלֶת</strong> (<em>memsheleth</em>) = domínio/governo sobre <strong>períodos temporais</strong>—NÃO domínio territorial</li><li>\"E as estrelas\" adicionado quase como adendo sintático—estrutura enfatiza os dois luminares</li><li><strong>עָשָׂה</strong> (<em>asah</em> = fez) usado, NÃO <strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = criou)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "17", "text": "E Deus os colocou no raqia, para alumiar sobre a terra.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>COLOCAÇÃO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Luzes colocadas <strong>NO</strong> raqia—contraste: aves voam <strong>SOBRE</strong> o raqia (v.20)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "18", "text": "E para dominar no dia e na noite, e para separar entre a luz e entre as trevas. E Deus viu que bom.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>INFINITIVOS DE PROPÓSITO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>\"Para dominar...e para separar\"—funções paralelas dos luminares</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "19", "text": "E foi tarde, e foi manhã, quarto dia.", "notes": []}, {"n": "20", "text": "E Deus disse: \"Pululem as águas enxames de seres vivos, e aves voem sobre a terra, sobre a face do raqia.\"", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - SERES VIVOS INTRODUZIDOS</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה</strong> (<em>nefesh chayah</em>) = ser vivo/seres vivos—literalmente \"respiração/garganta/alma viva\"; <strong>NÃO \"alma\" em sentido filosófico posterior</strong></li><li>Adicionado ao glossário; usado em vv.21, 24, 30</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>DUPLICAÇÃO DE RAIZ</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>שֶׁרֶץ</strong> (<em>sherets</em> = enxames) de <strong>יִשְׁרְצוּ</strong> (<em>yishretzu</em> = pululem)</li><li><strong>יְעוֹפֵף</strong> (<em>ye'ofef</em>) = forma duplicada/intensiva \"voando-voar\"</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>RELAÇÃO ESPACIAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Aves voam <strong>SOBRE a face do</strong> raqia—NÃO <strong>NO</strong> raqia (contraste: luzes <strong>NO</strong> raqia)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "21", "text": "E Deus criou as grandes criaturas marinhas, e todo ser vivo, os que se movem que as águas pulularam, segundo as suas espécies, e toda ave alada segundo a sua espécie. E Deus viu que bom.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - CRIOU, NÃO FEZ</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = criou) retorna pela primeira vez desde v.1—usado para seres vivos, NÃO para luzes ou plantas; sugere distinção de significância</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>CRIATURAS MARINHAS</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>תַּנִּינִים</strong> (<em>taninim</em>) = grandes criaturas marinhas/grandes animais aquáticos—evitando \"monstros marinhos\" ou \"dragões\" (sobreposição mitológica)</li><li><strong>לְמִינֵהֶם/לְמִינֵהוּ</strong> (<em>leminehem/leminehu</em>) = \"segundo suas espécies\"—padrão reprodutivo como em v.11</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "22", "text": "E Deus os abençoou, dizendo: \"Frutificai e multiplicai-vos, e enchei as águas nos mares, e multipliquem-se as aves na terra.\"", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>PRIMEIRA FÓRMULA DE BÊNÇÃO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>וַיְבָרֶךְ</strong> (<em>vayvarekh</em>) = \"e abençoou\" (primeira ocorrência)—recorrerá: v.28 (humanos), Gênesis 2:3 (sétimo dia)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>TRIPLO IMPERATIVO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>פְּרוּ</strong> (<em>peru</em>) = frutificai; <strong>וּרְבוּ</strong> (<em>urvu</em>) = multiplicai; <strong>וּמִלְאוּ</strong> (<em>umil'u</em>) = enchei</li><li><strong>לֵאמֹר</strong> (<em>lemor</em> = \"dizendo\") introduz discurso divino direto às criaturas—característica narrativa incomum</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "23", "text": "E foi tarde, e foi manhã, quinto dia.", "notes": []}, {"n": "24", "text": "E Deus disse: \"Produza a terra seres vivos segundo a sua espécie: gado e répteis e animais da terra, segundo a sua espécie.\" E foi assim.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>NEFESH CHAYAH - Animais Terrestres</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה</strong> agora aplicado a animais terrestres (anteriormente criaturas aquáticas, vv.20-21)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>TRÊS CATEGORIAS</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בְּהֵמָה</strong> (<em>behemah</em>) = gado; <strong>רֶמֶשׂ</strong> (<em>remes</em>) = répteis; <strong>חַיְתוֹ־אֶרֶץ</strong> (<em>chayeto-eretz</em>) = animais da terra/animais selvagens</li><li>Padrão paralelo à vegetação do Dia 3: terra traz adiante sob comando divino</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "25", "text": "E Deus fez os animais da terra segundo a sua espécie, e o gado segundo a sua espécie, e todo réptil do solo segundo a sua espécie. E Deus viu que bom.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>SOLO vs. TERRA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>אֲדָמָה</strong> (<em>adamah</em>) = solo (PRIMEIRA ocorrência)—distinto de <strong>אֶרֶץ</strong> (<em>eretz</em> = terra)</li><li><strong>עָשָׂה</strong> (<em>asah</em> = fez), NÃO <strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = criou)</li><li>Comando (v.24) → cumprimento (v.25) padrão como nos Dias 3-4</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "26", "text": "E Deus disse: \"Façamos <em>um</em> humano à nossa imagem, conforme a nossa semelhança, e dominem sobre os peixes do mar e sobre as aves do céu e sobre o gado e sobre toda a terra e sobre todo réptil que se move sobre a terra.\"", "notes": [{"type": "theological", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - DISCURSO DIVINO PLURAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Primeira pessoa <strong>PLURAL</strong>: \"<strong>façamos</strong>...à <strong>nossa</strong> imagem...<strong>nossa</strong> semelhança\"</li><li>Interpretações <strong>POSSÍVEIS</strong>: (1) plural majestático, (2) conselho divino, (3) plural literário</li><li>Nota marca <strong>INCERTEZA</strong>—NÃO impõe interpretação Trinitária</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>HUMANO = GENÉRICO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>אָדָם</strong> (<em>adam</em>) SEM artigo = humano/humanidade genérico—NÃO ainda nome próprio \"Adão\"</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>IMAGEM &amp; SEMELHANÇA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>צֶלֶם</strong> (<em>tselem</em>) = imagem; <strong>דְּמוּת</strong> (<em>demut</em>) = semelhança</li><li>Ambos = representação/semelhança; pareados para ênfase, NÃO significado idêntico</li><li><strong>Referência cruzada:</strong> O par reaparece em <strong>Gn 5:3</strong> — Adão gera Shet (Sete) \"em sua semelhança, conforme a sua imagem,\" invertendo a ordem divino-humana para descendência humano-humana. Para discussão mais completa, veja o companheiro Seção A12b.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>DOMÍNIO = GOVERNO FUNCIONAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>רָדָה</strong> (<em>radah</em>) = dominar/governar—autoridade funcional, <strong>NÃO propriedade</strong></li><li>Mudança de verbo: \"façamos UM humano\" (singular) → \"dominem\" (plural)</li><li><strong>הָרֶמֶשׂ הָֽרֹמֵשׂ</strong> (<em>haremes haromes</em>) = \"réptil que se move\" (duplicação de raiz)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "27", "text": "E Deus criou o humano à sua imagem; à imagem de Deus o criou; macho e fêmea os criou.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - TRIPLA ÊNFASE DE CRIAÇÃO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = criou) usado <strong>TRÊS VEZES</strong>—<strong>ÚNICA ocorrência</strong> de tripla repetição de verbo em um versículo; mostra máxima significância/ênfase</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>ESTRUTURA POÉTICA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Três cláusulas paralelas com <strong>bara</strong> ancorando cada—estilo literário elevado</li><li>Mudança singular/plural: \"o humano...o criou\" (SINGULAR) → \"macho e fêmea...os criou\" (PLURAL)—humanidade coletiva torna-se diferenciada</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>DIFERENCIAÇÃO BIOLÓGICA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>זָכָר וּנְקֵבָה</strong> (<em>zakhar unqevah</em>) = macho e fêmea—termos gramaticais para sexo biológico, NÃO papéis culturais de gênero</li><li><strong>הָאָדָם</strong> (<em>ha'adam</em>) = \"O humano\" (com artigo) vs. v.26 <strong>אָדָם</strong> (sem artigo)—<strong>POSSÍVEL</strong> ênfase</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "28", "text": "E Deus os abençoou, e Deus lhes disse: \"Frutificai e multiplicai-vos, e enchei a terra e sujeitai-a, e dominai sobre os peixes do mar e sobre as aves do céu e sobre todo animal que se move sobre a terra.\"", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>FÓRMULA DE BÊNÇÃO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Como v.22 (criaturas marinhas/aves), mas expandida para humanos com comandos adicionais</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CINCO IMPERATIVOS</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Frutificai, multiplicai, enchei, <strong>sujeitai</strong>, <strong>dominai</strong></li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>SUJEITAR = CULTIVAÇÃO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>כָּבַשׁ</strong> (<em>kabash</em>) = sujeitar/trazer sob cultivo—termo agrícola (aparece APENAS aqui em Gênesis 1); <strong>NÃO licença para exploração ou violência</strong></li><li><strong>רָדָה</strong> (<em>radah</em>) agora como imperativo—governo funcional sobre animais, NÃO propriedade absoluta</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>REFERÊNCIA CRUZADA: REPETIÇÃO PÓS-DILÚVIO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>O comando \"frutificai e multiplicai-vos e enchei a terra\" reaparece literalmente em <strong>Gn 9:1</strong> após o dilúvio — o mandato da criação renovado. A linguagem de domínio em 9:2 muda de tom (animais <em>temem</em> humanos) e a permissão dietética se expande (9:3). Para discussão mais completa, veja o companheiro Seção G5b.</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "29", "text": "E Deus disse: \"Eis que vos dei toda erva semeando semente que <em>está</em> sobre a face de toda a terra, e toda árvore em que <em>há</em> fruto de árvore semeando semente; a vós será para alimento.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>PARTÍCULA DE ATENÇÃO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>הִנֵּה</strong> (<em>hineh</em>) = \"eis\"—sinaliza anúncio importante</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>DUPLICAÇÃO DE RAIZ</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>זֹרֵעַ זֶרַע</strong> (<em>zorea zera</em>) = \"semeando semente\"—padrão de vv.11-12</li></ul>"}, {"type": "theological", "title": "<strong>DIETA ORIGINAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Vegetação APENAS para humanos—NENHUM consumo animal permitido ainda (contraste Gênesis 9:3 permissão pós-dilúvio)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "30", "text": "E a todo animal da terra e a toda ave do céu e a todo réptil sobre a terra, em que <em>há</em> ser vivo, toda erva verde para alimento.\" E foi assim.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>NEFESH CHAYAH = Qualificador</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה</strong> distingue animais com respiração/vida de plantas</li></ul>"}, {"type": "theological", "title": "<strong>DIETA VEGETARIANA UNIVERSAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>TODOS os seres vivos comem apenas plantas inicialmente—animais também vegetarianos na criação original</li><li><strong>יֶרֶק עֵשֶׂב</strong> (<em>yereq esev</em>) = erva verde/vegetação fresca</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "31", "text": "E Deus viu tudo o que havia feito, e eis que muito bom. E foi tarde, e foi manhã, o sexto dia.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - MUDANÇA DE AVALIAÇÃO: MUITO BOM</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>טוֹב מְאֹד</strong> (<em>tov me'od</em>) = \"MUITO bom\" vs. simples <strong>טוֹב</strong> (<em>tov</em> = \"bom\") em TODOS os dias anteriores</li><li><strong>ÚNICA ocorrência</strong> de \"muito bom\" no relato da criação—mostra avaliação positiva abrangente após criação humana</li><li><strong>ISTO NÃO É VARIAÇÃO ESTILÍSTICA—É SIGNIFICÂNCIA TEOLÓGICA</strong></li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>HINEH = Atenção</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>הִנֵּה</strong> (<em>hineh</em> = \"eis\") aparece com avaliação—chama atenção para bondade abrangente</li><li>\"Tudo o que havia feito\"—toda criação revisada</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - ARTIGO EM \"O SEXTO DIA\"</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יוֹם הַשִּׁשִּׁי</strong> (<em>yom hashishi</em>) = \"O sexto dia\" com artigo definido <strong>ה</strong></li><li><strong>ÚNICO entre todos seis dias</strong> (Dias 1-5 NÃO têm artigo)</li><li>Significância <strong>POSSÍVEL</strong>: ênfase de conclusão, importância da criação humana, ou preparação para o Shabat (Gênesis 2:1-3)</li><li><strong>Muitas traduções perdem esta distinção</strong></li></ul>"}]}], "glossary": {"headers": ["Hebraico", "Português", "Notas"], "rows": [["אֱלֹהִים", "Deus", "Forma plural, verbo singular"], ["אֶרֶץ", "terra", "\"Solo\" só quando claramente superfície"], ["אֲדָמָה", "solo", "Distinto de <em>eretz</em>"], ["שָׁמַיִם", "céu, céus", "NÃO \"Céu\" espiritual"], ["רָקִיעַ", "raqia", "Transliterado; v.8 = céu"], ["מַיִם", "águas <em>(padrão)</em> / água <em>(contextual)</em>", "Plural padrão onde o contexto é plural-significativo (corpos separados, ajuntamento de águas). Singular \"água\" contextual permitido onde \"águas\" importaria registro tradicional arcaico; testar por Regra 3. Toda mudança registrada."], ["רוּחַ", "vento/espírito", "Pode adicionar \"sopro\" nas notas"], ["תְהוֹם", "o abismo", "Evitar especulação"], ["תֹהוּ וָבֹהוּ", "caos e vazio", "Raro; significado incerto"], ["נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה", "ser(es) vivo(s)", "NÃO \"alma\" filosoficamente"], ["בָּרָא", "criou", "Criação divina; v.1, 21, 27"], ["עָשָׂה", "fez", "Formação; v.7, 16, 25"], ["צֶלֶם", "imagem", "Pareado com <em>demut</em>"], ["דְּמוּת", "semelhança", "Pareado com <em>tselem</em>"], ["אָדָם", "humano", "Genérico; \"Adão\" quando próprio"], ["רָדָה", "dominar", "Governo funcional"], ["כָּבַשׁ", "sujeitar", "Termo agrícola"]]}, "supplementary": [{"title": "RASTREAMENTO DE FÓRMULAS", "body": "<p><strong>Fórmulas Travadas (Múltiplas Ocorrências):</strong></p><ul><li>\"E Deus disse...\" (10x)</li><li>\"E foi assim\" (6x)</li><li>\"E Deus viu que bom\" (6x) + \"muito bom\" (1x em v.31)</li><li>\"E foi tarde, e foi manhã, [X] dia\" (6x)</li><li>\"E Deus os abençoou\" (2x: vv.22, 28)</li><li>\"Frutificai e multiplicai-vos\" (2x: vv.22, 28)</li></ul><p><strong>Variações Significativas:</strong></p><ul><li>v.5: \"um dia\" (cardinal) vs. vv.8,13,19,23,31 (ordinais)</li><li>v.31: \"muito bom\" (NÃO simples \"bom\") + \"O sexto dia\" (artigo único)</li></ul>"}, {"title": "PADRÕES DE DUPLICAÇÃO DE RAIZ", "body": "<p>Dispositivo poético hebraico mostrando geração interna:</p><ul><li>v.11-12: \"semeando semente\" (<strong>מַזְרִיעַ זֶרַע</strong>), \"fazendo fruto\" (<strong>עֹשֶׂה פְרִי</strong>)</li><li>v.20: \"enxames\" de \"pululem\"</li><li>v.26: \"réptil que se move\" (<strong>הָרֶמֶשׂ הָֽרֹמֵשׂ</strong>)</li><li>v.29: \"semeando semente\" (<strong>זֹרֵעַ זֶרַע</strong>)</li></ul><p><strong>Preservado apesar de soar repetitivo—estilo poético hebraico intencional.</strong></p>"}, {"title": "MUDANÇAS DE VERBO - CRIOU vs. FEZ", "body": "<table class=\"cmp\"><thead><tr><th>Versículo</th><th>Ação</th><th>Verbo</th><th>Hebraico</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>v.1</td><td>Céus e terra</td><td><strong>criou</strong></td><td><em>bara</em> בָּרָא</td></tr><tr><td>v.7</td><td>Raqia</td><td>fez</td><td><em>asah</em> עָשָׂה</td></tr><tr><td>v.16</td><td>Luminares</td><td>fez</td><td><em>asah</em></td></tr><tr><td>v.21</td><td>Criaturas marinhas &amp; seres vivos</td><td><strong>criou</strong></td><td><em>bara</em></td></tr><tr><td>v.25</td><td>Animais terrestres</td><td>fez</td><td><em>asah</em></td></tr><tr><td>v.27</td><td>Humano (3x ênfase)</td><td><strong>criou</strong></td><td><em>bara</em></td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Padrão:</strong> <em>Bara</em> (criou) para criação inicial, seres vivos, humanos. <em>Asah</em> (fez) para raqia, luminares, animais terrestres. O escopo preciso de <em>bara</em> (se implica criação do nada ou remodelação de material existente) é debatido (POSSÍVEL).</p><p><strong>FIM DE GÊNESIS 1 - A TRADUÇÃO TRANSPARENTE (PORTUGUÊS BRASILEIRO)</strong></p>"}]}, "de": {"verses": [{"n": "1", "text": "Im Anfang schuf Gott den Himmel und das Land.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>KRITISCH - Struktur &amp; Interpretation</strong>", "body": "<p>Hebräisch: <strong>בְּרֵאשִׁית בָּרָא אֱלֹהִים אֵת הַשָּׁמַיִם וְאֵת הָאָֽרֶץ</strong> (<em>Bereshit bara elohim et hashamayim ve'et ha'aretz</em>)</p><ul><li>Sieben-Wort-Struktur im Hebräischen (symbolische Zahl) geht in Übersetzung verloren</li><li><strong>בְּרֵאשִׁית</strong> (<em>bereshit</em>) = „in Anfang\" — im Hebräischen OHNE bestimmten Artikel. Die deutsche Wiedergabe „Im Anfang\" enthält den Artikel notwendigerweise (<em>im</em> = <em>in dem</em>), da „In Anfang\" nicht idiomatisch ist. Dies ist eine grammatisch erzwungene Abweichung gemäß Regel 17 (deutsche Artikel-Erweiterung), nicht interpretativ. Im Redaktionslog dokumentiert.</li><li>Grammatische Struktur erlaubt ZWEI Lesungen: (1) V.1 als eigenständiger Satz (traditionell, hier befolgt gemäß masoretischer Interpunktion), oder (2) V.1 als Titel/Überschrift mit Narrativbeginn V.2. <strong>MÖGLICH</strong>. Für ausführlichere Diskussion der Strukturoptionen siehe Begleitmaterial Abschnitt B.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>SCHLÜSSELBEGRIFFE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>אֵת</strong> (<em>et</em>) erscheint 2x—unübersetzbares Akkusativobjekt-Marker einzigartig im Hebräischen</li><li><strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em>) = wird distinktiv für göttliches Schöpfungshandeln verwendet; der genaue Umfang (ob Schöpfung aus dem Nichts oder Umgestaltung vorhandenen Materials) ist umstritten (MÖGLICH); unterscheidet sich von <strong>עָשָׂה</strong> (<em>asah</em> = machen/formen)</li><li><strong>שָׁמַיִם</strong> (<em>shamayim</em>) = physischer Himmel (Plural); NICHT geistliches „Himmelreich\"</li><li><strong>אֶרֶץ</strong> (<em>eretz</em>) = Land/Boden; NICHT Planet „Erde\"</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>DEUTSCHE BESONDERHEIT</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Alle Substantive großgeschrieben (deutsche Grammatik, nicht theologische Betonung)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "2", "text": "Und das Land war Chaos und Leere, und Finsternis <em>war</em> über der Fläche der Tiefe, und Wind/Geist Gottes schwebend über der Fläche der Wasser.", "notes": [{"type": "theological", "title": "<strong>AMBIGUITÄT BEWAHRT</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>תֹהוּ וָבֹהוּ</strong> (<em>tohu vavohu</em>) = seltene Phrase (erscheint nur 3x in der Bibel); genaue Bedeutung <strong>UNGEWISS</strong>; assoziiert mit Zerstörung/Verwüstung. „Chaos und Leere\" ist <strong>MÖGLICHE</strong> Übersetzung. Vermeiden Sie elaborate kosmologische Spekulation.</li><li><strong>רוּחַ אֱלֹהִים</strong> (<em>ruach elohim</em>) = Wind/Geist/Atem Gottes—ALLE DREI Bedeutungen vorhanden; grammatisch feminin im Hebräischen</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>SCHLÜSSELBEGRIFFE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>תְהוֹם</strong> (<em>tehom</em>) = die Tiefe/massiver Wasserkörper; <strong>WAHRSCHEINLICHE</strong> Übersetzung; vermeiden Sie „kosmischer Ozean\" (falsche Präzision)</li><li><strong>מְרַחֶפֶת</strong> (<em>merachefet</em>) = Partizip Präsens (fortlaufende Handlung)—NICHT einfaches Präteritum „schwebte\"; möglicherweise „brütend\" oder „bedeckend\"</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>GESCHLECHTSKONFLIKT (Hebräisch → Deutsch)</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>רוּחַ</strong> (<em>ruach</em>) ist grammatisch feminin im Hebräischen → <strong>der Wind/der Geist</strong> (maskulin) im Deutschen</li><li>Dies ist grammatisches Geschlecht, nicht ontologisches Attribut</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "3", "text": "Und Gott sprach: „Es werde Licht,\" und Licht war.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>JUSSIV &amp; VAV CONVERSIVUM</strong> (Hier erklärt; nicht wiederholt in späteren Versen)", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יְהִי</strong> (<em>yehi</em>) = Futur/Jussiv-Form als göttlicher Befehl—wörtlich „es werde\" statt Imperativ</li><li><strong>Konjunktiv I</strong> („Es werde Licht\") bewahrt hebräische Jussiv-Form in Transparenter Ausgabe</li><li><strong>Vav conversivum (ו)</strong> bei <strong>וַיְהִי</strong> (<em>vayehi</em>) wandelt Futur „es werde\" → narrative Vergangenheit „und war\"—einzigartiges biblisch-hebräisches Merkmal, das Narrativ vorantreibt. Dieses Muster setzt sich in Genesis 1 fort.</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "4", "text": "Und Gott sah das Licht, dass gut, und Gott trennte zwischen dem Licht und zwischen der Finsternis.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>KOMPRIMIERTE BEWERTUNG</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Hebräisch <strong>כִּי־טוֹב</strong> (<em>ki-tov</em>) = „dass gut\" ohne explizites „es war\"—Transparente Ausgabe bewahrt hebräische Kompression; Leserausgabe würde zu „dass es gut war\" erweitern</li><li>„Zwischen...und zwischen\" (<strong>בֵּין...וּבֵין</strong>) = hebräisches Wiederholungsmuster bewahrt; setzt sich fort in Vv.6, 7, 14, 18</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "5", "text": "Und Gott nannte das Licht „Tag\", und die Finsternis nannte er „Nacht\". Und <em>es</em> war Abend, und <em>es</em> war Morgen, Tag eins.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>KRITISCH - Tag EINS, Nicht ERSTER</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Hebräisch <strong>יוֹם אֶחָד</strong> (<em>yom echad</em>) = Kardinalzahl—NICHT Ordinalzahl <strong>רִאשׁוֹן</strong> (<em>rishon</em> = „erster\"). Tage 2-6 verwenden Ordinalzahlen (zweiter, dritter, vierter, fünfter, sechster). <strong>Tag 1 wird linguistisch anders behandelt—dies ist bedeutsam.</strong></li><li>✅ <strong>Entscheidung (2026-04-18):</strong> „Tag eins\" gewählt statt „ein Tag\". „Ein Tag\" liest sich idiomatisch unbestimmt („a day / irgendein Tag\"); „Tag eins\" gibt die Kardinal-Etikettierung klarer wieder und vermeidet die Verwechslung mit dem unbestimmten Artikel. Im Redaktionslog dokumentiert.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>TAGESABSCHLUSSFORMEL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>„Und es war Abend, und es war Morgen, [X] Tag\" = GESPERRTE Formel; wiederholt sich exakt in Vv.8, 13, 19, 23, 31</li><li>Abend-Morgen-Reihenfolge spiegelt hebräischen Tag wider, der bei Sonnenuntergang beginnt</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "6", "text": "Und Gott sprach: „Es werde <em>ein</em> raqia (Ausdehnung) innerhalb der Wasser, und <em>es</em> sei eine Scheidewand zwischen Wasser und Wasser.\"", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>KRITISCH - RAQIA-EINFÜHRUNG</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Hebräisch <strong>רָקִיעַ</strong> (<em>raqia</em>) von Wurzel <strong>ר-ק-ע</strong> = „hämmern/schlagen/ausbreiten\"—der semantische Bereich des Wortes ist umstritten; antike Ausleger verstanden es unterschiedlich als solides Gewölbe, atmosphärische Ausdehnung oder Grenzschicht</li><li><strong>TRANSLITERIERT</strong> in Genesis 1, um falsche kosmologische Präzision zu vermeiden</li><li>Vers 8 wird <strong>raqia = shamayim (Himmel)</strong> identifizieren</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>STRUKTUR</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בְּתוֹךְ</strong> (<em>betoch</em>) = „innerhalb/im Innern\" der Wasser (das raqia bildet sich innerhalb der Wassermasse)—nicht „mitten unter\"</li><li><strong>מַבְדִּיל</strong> (<em>mavdil</em>) = substantivisch gebrauchtes Hifil-Partizip: „eine Scheidewand\"—nicht das finite „trennt\" oder der Infinitiv „trennen\"</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "7", "text": "Und Gott machte das raqia, und er trennte zwischen den Wassern, die unter dem raqia <em>waren</em>, und zwischen den Wassern, die über dem raqia <em>waren</em>. Und <em>es</em> war so.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>VERBWECHSEL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = schuf, V.1) vs. <strong>עָשָׂה</strong> (<em>asah</em> = machte, V.7)—beide für göttliche Handlung verwendet; <strong>MÖGLICHER</strong> Unterschied zwischen den Verben; der genaue Umfang von <em>bara</em> (Schöpfung aus dem Nichts oder Umgestaltung vorhandenen Materials) ist umstritten</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>FORMEL EINGEFÜHRT</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>„Und es war so\" (<strong>וַיְהִי־כֵן</strong>) erscheint zum ersten Mal; wiederholt sich in Vv.9, 11, 15, 24, 30</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "8", "text": "Und Gott nannte das raqia „Himmel\". Und <em>es</em> war Abend, und <em>es</em> war Morgen, zweiter Tag.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>KRITISCH - RAQIA = HIMMEL-IDENTIFIKATION</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Gott identifiziert explizit <strong>raqia = shamayim (Himmel)</strong>—der Text verankert <em>raqia</em> im Bereich des sichtbaren Himmels. Der semantische Bereich von <em>raqia</em> (von der Wurzel „hämmern/ausbreiten\") bleibt unter Gelehrten umstritten; antike Ausleger verstanden es unterschiedlich als solides Gewölbe, atmosphärische Ausdehnung oder Grenzschicht. Diese Identifizierung legt den Himmelsbereich fest, ohne jene Fragen zu lösen.</li><li>Nachfolgende Verse mit „raqia\" (Vv.14-20) behalten diese Identifikation bei</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>TAG 2 ORDINALZAHL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יוֹם שֵׁנִי</strong> (<em>yom sheni</em>) = „zweiter Tag\" (Ordinalzahl)—anders als Tag 1's Kardinalzahl „ein\"</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "9", "text": "Und Gott sprach: „Die Wasser unter dem Himmel sollen sich sammeln an einen Ort, und das trockene <em>Land</em> werde gesehen.\" Und <em>es</em> war so.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>PASSIV BEWAHRT</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יִקָּווּ</strong> (<em>yikavu</em>) = „sollen sich sammeln\" (passiv); <strong>תֵרָאֶה</strong> (<em>teira'eh</em>) = „werde gesehen\" (passiv)—nicht aktive Befehle an die Wasser, sondern passive göttliche Verursachung</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>WORTWURZEL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יִקָּווּ</strong> von Wurzel <strong>ק-ו-ה</strong> (sammeln/ansammeln)—verwandt mit <strong>מִקְוֵה</strong> (<em>miqveh</em> = Ritualbad, Wasseransammlung)</li><li>Singular „Ort\" für Land (zusammenhängende Landmasse) antizipiert Plural „Meere\" V.10</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "10", "text": "Und Gott nannte das trockene <em>Land</em> „Land\", und die Ansammlung der Wasser nannte er „Meere\". Und Gott sah, dass gut.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>SINGULAR vs. PLURAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>אֶרֶץ</strong> (<em>eretz</em>) = Land (SINGULAR zusammenhängende Landmasse); <strong>יַמִּים</strong> (<em>yamim</em>) = Meere (PLURAL getrennte Wasserkörper)</li><li>Hebräisch unterscheidet ein Land von mehreren Meeren (Mittelmeer + Rotes Meer in der antiken Geographie getrennt)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "11", "text": "Und Gott sprach: „Das Land lasse grünen Grün, Kräuter samend Samen, Fruchtbäume Frucht-machend nach seiner Art, deren Samen in ihm <em>ist</em>, auf dem Land.\" Und <em>es</em> war so.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>SELTENES VERB - „GRÜNEN LASSEN\"</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>תַּדְשֵׁא</strong> (<em>tadsheh</em>) = Verb aus Substantiv <strong>דֶּשֶׁא</strong> (Grün/Gras) gebildet—ähnlich zu „grünen lassen\". JA, klingt ungewöhnlich—<strong>beabsichtigte Bewahrung des hebräischen poetischen Stils.</strong></li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>WURZELVERDOPPELUNGSMUSTER</strong> (hebräisches poetisches Mittel)", "body": "<ul><li><strong>מַזְרִיעַ זֶרַע</strong> (<em>mazria zera</em>) = „samend Samen\"; <strong>עֹשֶׂה פְרִי</strong> (<em>oseh pri</em>) = „Frucht-machend\"</li><li>Zeigt interne Produktion/Generation—<strong>bewahrt trotz Ungewöhnlichkeit</strong></li><li><strong>דֶּשֶׁא עֵשֶׂב</strong> (<em>deshe esev</em>) = „Grün, Kräuter\" (Synonym-Paarung für stilistische Wirkung)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>REPRODUKTIONSMUSTER</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>לְמִינוֹ</strong> (<em>lemino</em>) = „nach seiner Art/Typ\"—beschreibt Reproduktionsmuster</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "12", "text": "Und das Land brachte hervor Grün, Kräuter samend Samen nach ihrer Art, und Bäume Frucht-machend, deren Samen in ihm <em>ist</em>, nach ihrer Art. Und Gott sah, dass gut.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>BEFEHL → ERFÜLLUNGSMUSTER</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>V.11 Befehl → V.12 Erfüllung mit nahezu identischem Wortlaut—zeigt exakte Übereinstimmung</li><li>Wurzelverdopplung beibehalten: „samend Samen\", „Frucht-machend\"</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "13", "text": "Und <em>es</em> war Abend, und <em>es</em> war Morgen, dritter Tag.", "notes": []}, {"n": "14", "text": "Und Gott sprach: „Es sollen sein Lichter im raqia, zu trennen zwischen dem Tag und zwischen der Nacht, und sie sollen sein für Zeichen und für bestimmte Zeiten und für Tage und Jahre.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>LICHTKÖRPER EINGEFÜHRT</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>מְאֹרֹת</strong> (<em>me'orot</em>) = Lichter/Leuchtkörper/Lichtträger von Wurzel <strong>א-ו-ר</strong> (Licht)—Plural, aber spezifische Referenten unbenannt bis V.16</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>RAQIA-REFERENZ</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Nach V.8 wurde <em>raqia</em> mit <em>shamayim</em> (Himmel) identifiziert; dieser Vers platziert die Lichter „im raqia\" und bestätigt damit die Identifikation</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>BESTIMMTE ZEITEN</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>מוֹעֲדִים</strong> (<em>mo'adim</em>) = bestimmte Zeiten/Jahreszeiten/Feste—kann natürliche Jahreszeiten ODER heilige Kalenderereignisse bedeuten; Bedeutungsbereich bewahrt</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "15", "text": "Und sie sollen sein für Lichter im raqia, zu leuchten auf das Land.\" Und <em>es</em> war so.", "notes": []}, {"n": "16", "text": "Und Gott machte die zwei großen Lichter: das größere Licht für die Herrschaft des Tages, und das kleinere Licht für die Herrschaft der Nacht, und die Sterne.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>KRITISCH - UNBENANNTE LICHTKÖRPER</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Sonne und Mond <strong>UNBENANNT GELASSEN</strong>—nur als „größeres Licht\" und „kleineres Licht\" beschrieben</li><li>Altorientalischer Kontext: Vermeidung von Gottheitsnamen aus umgebenden Kulturen</li><li>Transparente Ausgabe widersteht namentlicher Identifikation</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>HERRSCHAFT = ZEITLICHE REGEL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>מֶמְשֶׁלֶת</strong> (<em>memsheleth</em>) = Herrschaft/Regel über <strong>Zeitperioden</strong>—NICHT territoriale Herrschaft</li><li>„Und die Sterne\" fast als syntaktischer Nachtrag hinzugefügt—Struktur betont die zwei Lichter</li><li><strong>עָשָׂה</strong> (<em>asah</em> = machte) verwendet, NICHT <strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = schuf)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "17", "text": "Und Gott setzte sie in das raqia, zu leuchten auf das Land.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>PLATZIERUNG</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Lichter platziert <strong>IM</strong> raqia—Kontrast: Vögel fliegen <strong>ÜBER</strong> das raqia (V.20)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "18", "text": "Und zu herrschen am Tag und in der Nacht, und zu trennen zwischen dem Licht und zwischen der Finsternis. Und Gott sah, dass gut.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>ZWECK-INFINITIVE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>„Zu herrschen...und zu trennen\"—parallele Funktionen der Lichter</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "19", "text": "Und <em>es</em> war Abend, und <em>es</em> war Morgen, vierter Tag.", "notes": []}, {"n": "20", "text": "Und Gott sprach: „Die Wasser sollen wimmeln <em>von</em> Gewimmel lebendiger Wesen, und Vögel sollen fliegen über das Land, über der Fläche des raqia.\"", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>KRITISCH - LEBENDIGE WESEN EINGEFÜHRT</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה</strong> (<em>nefesh chayah</em>) = lebendiges Wesen/lebendige Wesen—wörtlich „lebendiger Atem/Kehle/Seele\"; <strong>NICHT „Seele\" im späteren philosophischen Sinne</strong></li><li>Zum Glossar hinzugefügt; verwendet in Vv.21, 24, 30</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>WURZELVERDOPPLUNG</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>שֶׁרֶץ</strong> (<em>sherets</em> = Gewimmel) von <strong>יִשְׁרְצוּ</strong> (<em>yishretzu</em> = sollen wimmeln)</li><li><strong>יְעוֹפֵף</strong> (<em>ye'ofef</em>) = verdoppelte/intensive Form „fliegend-fliegen\"</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>RÄUMLICHE BEZIEHUNG</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Vögel fliegen <strong>ÜBER der Fläche des</strong> raqia—NICHT <strong>IM</strong> raqia (Kontrast: Lichter <strong>IM</strong> raqia)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "21", "text": "Und Gott schuf die großen Meeresgeschöpfe, und jedes lebendige Wesen, die sich bewegenden, <em>die</em> die Wasser wimmelten, nach ihren Arten, und jeden beflügelten Vogel nach seiner Art. Und Gott sah, dass gut.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>KRITISCH - GESCHAFFEN, NICHT GEMACHT</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = schuf) kehrt zum ersten Mal seit V.1 zurück—verwendet für lebendige Wesen, NICHT für Lichter oder Pflanzen; deutet auf Bedeutungsunterschied hin</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>MEERESGESCHÖPFE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>תַּנִּינִים</strong> (<em>taninim</em>) = große Meeresgeschöpfe/große Wassertiere—vermeiden Sie „Seeungeheuer\" oder „Drachen\" (mythologische Überlagerung)</li><li><strong>לְמִינֵהֶם/לְמִינֵהוּ</strong> (<em>leminehem/leminehu</em>) = „nach ihren Arten\"—Reproduktionsmuster wie in V.11</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "22", "text": "Und Gott segnete sie, sagend: „Seid fruchtbar und mehret euch, und füllet die Wasser in den Meeren, und die Vögel sollen sich mehren auf dem Land.\"", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>ERSTE SEGENSFORMEL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>וַיְבָרֶךְ</strong> (<em>vayvarekh</em>) = „und er segnete\" (erstes Auftreten)—wird wiederkehren: V.28 (Menschen), Genesis 2:3 (siebter Tag)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>DREIFACHER IMPERATIV</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>פְּרוּ</strong> (<em>peru</em>) = seid fruchtbar; <strong>וּרְבוּ</strong> (<em>urvu</em>) = mehret euch; <strong>וּמִלְאוּ</strong> (<em>umil'u</em>) = füllet</li><li><strong>לֵאמֹר</strong> (<em>lemor</em> = „sagend\") führt direkte göttliche Rede zu Geschöpfen ein—ungewöhnliches narratives Merkmal</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "23", "text": "Und <em>es</em> war Abend, und <em>es</em> war Morgen, fünfter Tag.", "notes": []}, {"n": "24", "text": "Und Gott sprach: „Das Land bringe hervor lebendige Wesen nach ihrer Art: Vieh und kriechende Dinge und Lebewesen des Landes, nach ihrer Art.\" Und <em>es</em> war so.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>NEFESH CHAYAH - Landtiere</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה</strong> jetzt angewendet auf Landtiere (zuvor Wassergeschöpfe, Vv.20-21)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>DREI KATEGORIEN</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בְּהֵמָה</strong> (<em>behemah</em>) = Vieh; <strong>רֶמֶשׂ</strong> (<em>remes</em>) = kriechende Dinge; <strong>חַיְתוֹ־אֶרֶץ</strong> (<em>chayeto-eretz</em>) = Lebewesen des Landes/wilde Tiere</li><li>Muster parallel zu Tag 3 Vegetation: Land bringt hervor auf göttlichen Befehl</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "25", "text": "Und Gott machte die Lebewesen des Landes nach ihrer Art, und das Vieh nach seiner Art, und jedes kriechende Ding des Bodens nach seiner Art. Und Gott sah, dass gut.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>BODEN vs. LAND</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>אֲדָמָה</strong> (<em>adamah</em>) = Boden/Erde (ERSTES Auftreten)—unterscheidet sich von <strong>אֶרֶץ</strong> (<em>eretz</em> = Land)</li><li><strong>עָשָׂה</strong> (<em>asah</em> = machte), NICHT <strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = schuf)</li><li>Befehl (V.24) → Erfüllung (V.25) Muster wie an Tagen 3-4</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>GESCHLECHTSKONFLIKT</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>אֶרֶץ</strong> (<em>eretz</em>) ist feminin im Hebräischen → <strong>das Land</strong> (neutral) im Deutschen</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "26", "text": "Und Gott sprach: „Lasst uns <em>einen</em> Menschen machen in unserem Bild, nach unserer Ähnlichkeit, und sie sollen herrschen über die Fische des Meeres und über die Vögel des Himmels und über das Vieh und über das ganze Land und über jedes kriechende Ding, <em>das</em> kriecht auf dem Land.\"", "notes": [{"type": "theological", "title": "<strong>KRITISCH - PLURALE GÖTTLICHE REDE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Erste Person <strong>PLURAL</strong>: „Lasst <strong>uns</strong> machen...in <strong>unserem</strong> Bild...<strong>unserer</strong> Ähnlichkeit\"</li><li><strong>MÖGLICHE</strong> Interpretationen: (1) Pluralis Majestatis, (2) göttlicher Rat, (3) literarischer Plural</li><li>Notiz markiert <strong>UNGEWISSHEIT</strong>—setzt KEINE Trinitätslehre voraus</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>MENSCH = GENERISCH</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>אָדָם</strong> (<em>adam</em>) OHNE Artikel = generischer Mensch/Menschheit—NOCH NICHT Eigenname „Adam\"</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>BILD &amp; ÄHNLICHKEIT</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>צֶלֶם</strong> (<em>tselem</em>) = Bild; <strong>דְּמוּת</strong> (<em>demut</em>) = Ähnlichkeit</li><li>Beide = Repräsentation/Ähnlichkeit; gepaart für Betonung, NICHT identische Bedeutung</li><li><strong>Querverweis:</strong> Das Paar erscheint erneut in <strong>Gn 5:1–3</strong>, wo gesagt wird, dass Adam den Seth <em>„in seiner Ähnlichkeit, nach seinem Bild\"</em> zeugte—die göttlich-menschliche Reihenfolge wird zur menschlich-menschlichen Abstammung umgekehrt und die Schöpfungssprache durch die Generationen verkettet.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>HERRSCHAFT = FUNKTIONALE REGEL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>רָדָה</strong> (<em>radah</em>) = herrschen/regieren—funktionale Autorität, <strong>NICHT Eigentum</strong></li><li>Verbwechsel: „macht EINEN Menschen\" (Singular) → „sie sollen herrschen\" (Plural)</li><li><strong>הָרֶמֶשׂ הָֽרֹמֵשׂ</strong> (<em>haremes haromes</em>) = „kriechende Ding, das kriecht\" (Wurzelverdopplung)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "27", "text": "Und Gott schuf den Menschen in seinem Bild; im Bild Gottes schuf er ihn; männlich und weiblich schuf er sie.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>KRITISCH - DREIFACHE SCHÖPFUNGSBETONUNG</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = schuf) <strong>DREIMAL</strong> verwendet—<strong>EINZIGES Auftreten</strong> dreifacher Verbwiederholung in einem Vers; zeigt maximale Bedeutung/Betonung</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>POETISCHE STRUKTUR</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Drei parallele Klauseln mit <strong>bara</strong> als Anker für jede—erhobener literarischer Stil</li><li>Singular/Plural-Wechsel: „den Menschen...ihn\" (SINGULAR) → „männlich und weiblich...sie\" (PLURAL)—kollektive Menschheit wird differenziert</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>BIOLOGISCHE DIFFERENZIERUNG</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>זָכָר וּנְקֵבָה</strong> (<em>zakhar unqevah</em>) = männlich und weiblich—grammatische Begriffe für biologisches Geschlecht, NICHT Geschlechterrollen</li><li><strong>הָאָדָם</strong> (<em>ha'adam</em>) = „DER Mensch\" (mit Artikel) vs. V.26 <strong>אָדָם</strong> (ohne Artikel)—<strong>MÖGLICHE</strong> Betonung</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "28", "text": "Und Gott segnete sie, und Gott sprach zu ihnen: „Seid fruchtbar und mehret euch, und füllet das Land und unterwerfet es, und herrschet über die Fische des Meeres und über die Vögel des Himmels und über jedes Lebewesen, <em>das</em> sich bewegt auf dem Land.\"", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>SEGENSFORMEL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Wie V.22 (Meeresgeschöpfe/Vögel), aber erweitert für Menschen mit zusätzlichen Befehlen</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>FÜNF IMPERATIVE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Seid fruchtbar, mehret euch, füllet, <strong>unterwerfet</strong>, <strong>herrschet</strong></li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>UNTERWERFEN = KULTIVIERUNG</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>כָּבַשׁ</strong> (<em>kabash</em>) = unterwerfen/unter Kultivierung bringen—landwirtschaftlicher Begriff (erscheint NUR hier in Genesis 1); <strong>NICHT Lizenz für Ausbeutung oder Gewalt</strong></li><li><strong>רָדָה</strong> (<em>radah</em>) jetzt als Imperativ—funktionale Herrschaft über Tiere, NICHT absolutes Eigentum</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>QUERVERWEIS: NACH-FLUT-WIEDERHOLUNG</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Der Befehl „seid fruchtbar und mehret euch und füllet das Land\" erscheint wörtlich erneut in <strong>Gn 9:1</strong>—das Schöpfungsmandat nach der Flut erneuert, aber mit veränderter ökologischer Beziehung. Für ausführlichere Diskussion der Parallelen und Unterschiede (Gn 9:2–3) siehe Begleitmaterial Abschnitt C.</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "29", "text": "Und Gott sprach: „Siehe, ich habe euch gegeben jedes Kraut samend Samen, <em>das</em> auf der Fläche des ganzen Landes <em>ist</em>, und jeden Baum, in dem <em>ist</em> Frucht <em>eines</em> Baumes samend Samen; euch soll <em>es</em> sein zur Nahrung.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>AUFMERKSAMKEITSPARTIKEL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>הִנֵּה</strong> (<em>hineh</em>) = „siehe\"—signalisiert wichtige Ankündigung</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>WURZELVERDOPPLUNG</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>זֹרֵעַ זֶרַע</strong> (<em>zorea zera</em>) = „samend Samen\"—Muster von Vv.11-12</li></ul>"}, {"type": "theological", "title": "<strong>URSPRÜNGLICHE ERNÄHRUNG</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Vegetation NUR für Menschen—KEIN Tierkonsum erlaubt bisher (Kontrast Genesis 9:3 Nach-Flut-Erlaubnis)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "30", "text": "Und jedem Lebewesen des Landes und jedem Vogel des Himmels und allem Kriechenden auf dem Land, in dem <em>ein</em> lebendiges Wesen <em>ist</em>, jedes grüne Kraut zur Nahrung.\" Und <em>es</em> war so.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>NEFESH CHAYAH = Qualifikator</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה</strong> unterscheidet Tiere mit Atem/Leben von Pflanzen</li></ul>"}, {"type": "theological", "title": "<strong>UNIVERSELLE VEGETARISCHE ERNÄHRUNG</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>ALLE lebendigen Wesen essen anfänglich nur Pflanzen—Tiere auch vegetarisch in ursprünglicher Schöpfung</li><li><strong>יֶרֶק עֵשֶׂב</strong> (<em>yereq esev</em>) = grünes Kraut/frische Vegetation</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "31", "text": "Und Gott sah alles, was er gemacht hatte, und siehe, <em>es war</em> sehr gut. Und <em>es</em> war Abend, und <em>es</em> war Morgen, der sechste Tag.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>KRITISCH - BEWERTUNGSWECHSEL: SEHR GUT</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>טוֹב מְאֹד</strong> (<em>tov me'od</em>) = „SEHR gut\" vs. einfaches <strong>טוֹב</strong> (<em>tov</em> = „gut\") in ALLEN vorherigen Tagen</li><li><strong>EINZIGES Auftreten</strong> von „sehr gut\" im Schöpfungsbericht—zeigt umfassende positive Bewertung nach menschlicher Schöpfung</li><li><strong>DIES IST KEINE STILISTISCHE VARIATION—ES IST THEOLOGISCHE BEDEUTUNG</strong></li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>HINEH = Aufmerksamkeit</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>הִנֵּה</strong> (<em>hineh</em> = „siehe\") erscheint mit Bewertung—lenkt Aufmerksamkeit auf umfassende Güte</li><li>„Alles, was er gemacht hatte\"—gesamte Schöpfung überprüft</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>KRITISCH - ARTIKEL BEI „DER SECHSTE TAG\"</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יוֹם הַשִּׁשִּׁי</strong> (<em>yom hashishi</em>) = „DER sechste Tag\" mit bestimmtem Artikel <strong>ה</strong></li><li><strong>EINZIGARTIG unter allen sechs Tagen</strong> (Tage 1-5 haben KEINEN Artikel)</li><li><strong>MÖGLICHE</strong> Bedeutung: Abschlussbetonung, Wichtigkeit der menschlichen Schöpfung, oder Vorbereitung auf Sabbat (Genesis 2:1-3)</li><li><strong>Viele Übersetzungen verpassen diese Unterscheidung</strong></li></ul>"}]}], "glossary": {"headers": ["Hebräisch", "Deutsch", "Notizen"], "rows": [["אֱלֹהִים", "Gott", "Pluralform, Singular-Verb"], ["אֶרֶץ", "Land", "„Boden\" nur wenn eindeutig Erde/Boden"], ["אֲדָמָה", "Boden, Erde", "Unterscheidet sich von <em>eretz</em>"], ["שָׁמַיִם", "Himmel", "NICHT „Himmelreich\""], ["רָקִיעַ", "raqia", "Transliteriert; V.8 = Himmel"], ["מַיִם", "Wasser", "Singular im Deutschen, Plural im Hebräischen"], ["רוּחַ", "Wind/Geist", "Fem. HE → Mask. DE; Geschlechtskonflikt"], ["תְהוֹם", "die Tiefe", "Fem. in beiden Sprachen"], ["תֹהוּ וָבֹהוּ", "Chaos und Leere", "Selten; unsichere Bedeutung"], ["נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה", "lebendiges Wesen", "NICHT „Seele\" philosophisch"], ["בָּרָא", "schuf", "Göttliche Schöpfung; V.1, 21, 27"], ["עָשָׂה", "machte", "Formung; V.7, 16, 25"], ["צֶלֶם", "Bild", "Gepaart mit <em>demut</em>"], ["דְּמוּת", "Ähnlichkeit", "Gepaart mit <em>tselem</em>"], ["אָדָם", "Mensch", "Generisch; „Adam\" wenn Eigenname"], ["רָדָה", "herrschen", "Funktionale Herrschaft"], ["כָּבַשׁ", "unterwerfen", "Landwirtschaftlicher Begriff"]]}, "supplementary": [{"title": "FORMELVERFOLGUNG", "body": "<p><strong>Gesperrte Formeln (Mehrfaches Auftreten):</strong></p><ul><li>„Und Gott sprach...\" (10x) — Transparente Ausgabe nach Regel 7 (v2.4); Leserausgabe würde „sagte\" verwenden</li><li>„Und es war so\" (6x)</li><li>„Und Gott sah, dass gut\" (6x) + „sehr gut\" (1x bei V.31)</li><li>„Und es war Abend, und es war Morgen, [X] Tag\" (6x)</li><li>„Und Gott segnete sie\" (2x: Vv.22, 28)</li><li>„Seid fruchtbar und mehret euch\" (2x: Vv.22, 28)</li></ul><p><strong>Bedeutende Variationen:</strong></p><ul><li>V.5: „Tag eins\" (Kardinal) vs. Vv.8,13,19,23,31 (Ordinalzahlen)</li><li>V.31: „sehr gut\" (NICHT einfaches „gut\") + „DER sechste Tag\" (Artikel einzigartig)</li></ul>"}, {"title": "WURZELVERDOPPELUNGSMUSTER", "body": "<p>Hebräisches poetisches Mittel, das interne Generation zeigt:</p><ul><li>V.11-12: „samend Samen\" (<strong>מַזְרִיעַ זֶרַע</strong>), „Frucht-machend\" (<strong>עֹשֶׂה פְרִי</strong>)</li><li>V.20: „Gewimmel\" von „wimmeln\"</li><li>V.26: „kriechende Ding, das kriecht\" (<strong>הָרֶמֶשׂ הָֽרֹמֵשׂ</strong>)</li><li>V.29: „samend Samen\" (<strong>זֹרֵעַ זֶרַע</strong>)</li></ul><p><strong>Bewahrt trotz ungewöhnlichem Klang—beabsichtigter hebräischer poetischer Stil.</strong></p>"}, {"title": "VERBWECHSEL - GESCHAFFEN vs. GEMACHT", "body": "<table class=\"cmp\"><thead><tr><th>Vers</th><th>Handlung</th><th>Verb</th><th>Hebräisch</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>V.1</td><td>Himmel und Land</td><td><strong>schuf</strong></td><td><em>bara</em> בָּרָא</td></tr><tr><td>V.7</td><td>Raqia</td><td>machte</td><td><em>asah</em> עָשָׂה</td></tr><tr><td>V.16</td><td>Lichter</td><td>machte</td><td><em>asah</em></td></tr><tr><td>V.21</td><td>Meeresgeschöpfe &amp; lebendige Wesen</td><td><strong>schuf</strong></td><td><em>bara</em></td></tr><tr><td>V.25</td><td>Landtiere</td><td>machte</td><td><em>asah</em></td></tr><tr><td>V.27</td><td>Mensch (3x Betonung)</td><td><strong>schuf</strong></td><td><em>bara</em></td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Muster:</strong> <em>Bara</em> (schuf) für anfängliche Schöpfung, lebendige Wesen, Menschen. <em>Asah</em> (machte) für raqia, Lichter, Landtiere. <strong>MÖGLICHER</strong> Unterschied zwischen den Verben; der genaue Umfang von <em>bara</em> (Schöpfung aus dem Nichts oder Umgestaltung vorhandenen Materials) ist umstritten.</p>"}, {"title": "DEUTSCHE GRAMMATISCHE BESONDERHEITEN", "body": "<p><strong>Großschreibung:</strong></p><ul><li>Alle Substantive großgeschrieben (deutsche Grammatik)</li><li>NICHT theologische Betonung</li></ul><p><strong>Geschlechtskonflikte dokumentiert:</strong></p><ul><li>רוּחַ (fem.) → Wind/Geist (mask.)</li><li>אֶרֶץ (fem.) → Land (neutr.)</li></ul><p><strong>Konjunktiv I verwendet:</strong></p><ul><li>„Es werde Licht\" (V.3) - bewahrt hebräischen Jussiv</li><li>Transparente Ausgabe: Konjunktiv I beibehalten</li></ul><p><strong>ENDE VON GENESIS 1 - DIE TRANSPARENTE ÜBERSETZUNG (DEUTSCH)</strong></p>"}]}, "es": {"verses": [{"n": "1", "text": "En principio, Dios creó los cielos y la tierra.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - Estructura e Interpretacion</strong>", "body": "<p>Hebreo: <strong>בְּרֵאשִׁית בָּרָא אֱלֹהִים אֵת הַשָּׁמַיִם וְאֵת הָאָֽרֶץ</strong> (<em>Bereshit bara elohim et hashamayim ve'et ha'aretz</em>)</p><ul><li><strong>בְּרֵאשִׁית</strong> (<em>bereshit</em>) = \"en principio\" (SIN artículo--no \"en EL principio\")</li><li>La estructura gramatical permite DOS lecturas: (1) v.1 como oración independiente (tradicional, seguida aquí según puntuación masoretica), o (2) v.1 como titulo/superscripción con narrativa comenzando en v.2. <strong>POSIBLE</strong> que v.1 funcióne como encabezado del capítulo.</li></ul><p>Para una discusión más completa, vea el compañero Sección A.</p>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>TERMINOS CLAVE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em>) = término específico de creación divina; su alcance preciso (si implica creación de la nada o remodelación de material existente) es debatido (<strong>POSIBLE</strong>); distinto de <strong>עָשָׂה</strong> (<em>asah</em> = hacer/formar)</li><li><strong>שָׁמַיִם</strong> (<em>shamayim</em>) = cielo físico (plural); NO \"Cielo\" espíritual</li><li><strong>אֶרֶץ</strong> (<em>eretz</em>) = tierra/suelo; NO el planeta \"Tierra\"</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "2", "text": "Y la tierra era caos y vacío, y tinieblas sobre la faz del abismo, y viento/espíritu de Dios <em>se cernia</em> sobre la faz de las aguas.", "notes": [{"type": "theological", "title": "<strong>AMBIGUEDAD PRESERVADA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>תֹהוּ וָבֹהוּ</strong> (<em>tohu vavohu</em>) = frase rara (aparece solo 3 veces en la Biblia); significado exacto <strong>INCIERTO</strong>; asociada con destrucción/desolación. \"Caos y vacío\" es traducción <strong>POSIBLE</strong>. Evitar especulación cosmológica elaborada.</li><li><strong>רוּחַ אֱלֹהִים</strong> (<em>ruach elohim</em>) = viento/espíritu/aliento de Dios--las TRES acepciones presentes; gramaticalmente femenino en hebreo. <strong>Nota ES:</strong> <em>ruach</em> es femenino en hebreo pero <em>espíritu</em> es masculino en español y <em>viento</em> es masculino; el cambio de género es inevitable en la traducción.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>TERMINOS CLAVE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>תְהוֹם</strong> (<em>tehom</em>) = el abismo/masa de agua profunda; traducción <strong>PROBABLE</strong>; evitar \"oceano cósmico\" (falsa precision). <strong>Nota ES:</strong> <em>tehom</em> es femenino en hebreo; <em>abismo</em> es masculino en español.</li><li><strong>מְרַחֶפֶת</strong> (<em>merachefet</em>) = participio presente (acción continua)--NO preterito simple; posiblemente \"empollando\" o \"cubriendo\"</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "3", "text": "Y Dios dijo: \"Haya luz,\" y luz fue.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>YUSIVO Y VAV CONVERSIVO</strong> (Explicado aquí; no se repite en versículos posteriores)", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יְהִי</strong> (<em>yehi</em>) = forma futura/yusiva usada como mandato divino--literalmente \"haya\" en español, el subjuntivo desnudo preserva la fuerza del yusivo hebreo</li><li><strong>Vav conversivo (ו)</strong> en <strong>וַיְהִי</strong> (<em>vayehi</em>) cambia futuro \"habra\" a narrativo pasado \"y fue\"--característica única del hebreo bíblico que impulsa la narrativa. Este patron continua a lo largo de Génesis 1.</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "4", "text": "Y Dios vio la luz, que bueno, y Dios separó entre la luz y entre las tinieblas.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>EVALUACION COMPRIMIDA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Hebreo <strong>כִּי־טוֹב</strong> (<em>ki-tov</em>) = \"que bueno\" sin explícito \"era\"--la Edición Transparente preserva la compresion hebrea; una Edición de Lectura expandiria a \"que era bueno\"</li><li>\"Entre...y entre\" (<strong>בֵּין...וּבֵין</strong>) = patron repetitivo hebreo preservado; continua en vv.6, 7, 14, 18</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "5", "text": "Y Dios llamó a la luz \"Día,\" y a las tinieblas llamó \"Noche.\" Y fue tarde, y fue mañana, día uno.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - Día UNO, No PRIMERO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Hebreo <strong>יוֹם אֶחָד</strong> (<em>yom echad</em>) = \"día UNO\" (número cardinal)--NO ordinal <strong>רִאשׁוֹן</strong> (<em>rishon</em> = \"primero\"). Los días 2-6 usan ordinales (segundo, tercero, cuarto, quinto, sexto). <strong>El día 1 es tratado de forma diferente lingüísticamente--esto es significativo.</strong></li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>FORMULA DE CIERRE DEL DIA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>\"Y fue tarde, y fue mañana, [X] día\" = formula FIJA; se repite exactamente en vv.8, 13, 19, 23, 31</li><li>El orden tarde-mañana refleja el día hebreo comenzando al atardecer</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "6", "text": "Y Dios dijo: \"Haya <em>un</em> raqia (extensión) dentro de las aguas, y sea un separador entre aguas y aguas.\"", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - INTRODUCCIÓN DEL RAQIA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Hebreo <strong>רָקִיעַ</strong> (<em>raqia</em>) de la raíz <strong>ר-ק-ע</strong> = \"martillar/batir\"--describe una estructura martillada o batida</li><li><strong>TRANSLITERADO</strong> a lo largo de Génesis 1 para evitar falsa precision cosmológica</li><li>El versículo 8 identificara <strong>raqia = shamayim (cielo)</strong></li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>ESTRUCTURA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בְּתוֹךְ</strong> (<em>betoch</em>) = \"dentro\" de las aguas (el raqia se forma dentro de la masa de agua)—no \"en medio de/entre\"</li><li><strong>מַבְדִּיל</strong> (<em>mavdil</em>) = participio Hifil usado sustantivamente: \"un separador/divisor\"—no el finito \"separa\" ni el infinitivo \"separar\"</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "7", "text": "Y Dios hizo el raqia, y separó entre las aguas que <em>estaban</em> debajo del raqia y entre las aguas que <em>estaban</em> sobre el raqia. Y fue así.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>CAMBIO DE VERBO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = creo, v.1) vs. <strong>עָשָׂה</strong> (<em>asah</em> = hizo, v.7)--ambos usados para acción divina; <em>bara</em> se usa distintivamente para la acción creativa divina; su alcance preciso (si implica creación de la nada o remodelación de material existente) es debatido (<strong>POSIBLE</strong>)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>FORMULA INTRODUCIDA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>\"Y fue así\" (<strong>וַיְהִי־כֵן</strong>) aparece por primera vez; se repite en vv.9, 11, 15, 24, 30</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "8", "text": "Y Dios llamó al raqia \"Cielo.\" Y fue tarde, y fue mañana, segundo día.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - IDENTIFICACION RAQIA = CIELO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Dios identifica explícitamente <strong>raqia = shamayim (cielo)</strong> — el texto ancla el término sin resolver su rango semántico (bóveda sólida, expansión atmosférica, capa limitante). Los versículos subsiguientes (vv.14-20) mantienen esta identificación.</li><li>Para una discusión más completa sobre cosmología del <em>raqia</em>, vea el compañero Sección B.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>DIA 2 ORDINAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יוֹם שֵׁנִי</strong> (<em>yom sheni</em>) = \"segundo día\" (ordinal)--a diferencia del cardinal \"uno\" del Día 1</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "9", "text": "Y Dios dijo: \"Sean reunidas las aguas de debajo del cielo a un lugar, y sea vista la tierra seca.\" Y fue así.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>VOZ PASIVA PRESERVADA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יִקָּווּ</strong> (<em>yikavu</em>) = \"sean reunidas\" (pasivo); <strong>תֵרָאֶה</strong> (<em>teira'eh</em>) = \"sea vista\" (pasivo)--no mandatos activos a las aguas, sino causación divina pasiva</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>RAIZ DE LA PALABRA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יִקָּווּ</strong> de la raíz <strong>ק-ו-ה</strong> (reunir/juntar)--relaciónada con <strong>מִקְוֵה</strong> (<em>miqveh</em> = bano ritual, reunión de aguas)</li><li>\"Lugar\" singular para la tierra (masa terrestre conectada) anticipa \"mares\" plural v.10</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "10", "text": "Y Dios llamó a la tierra seca \"Tierra,\" y a la reunión de las aguas llamó \"Mares.\" Y Dios vio que bueno.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>SINGULAR vs. PLURAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>אֶרֶץ</strong> (<em>eretz</em>) = tierra (SINGULAR masa terrestre conectada); <strong>יַמִּים</strong> (<em>yamim</em>) = mares (PLURAL cuerpos de agua separados)</li><li>El hebreo distingue una tierra de multiples mares (Mediterraneo + Mar Rojo separados en la geografía antigua)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "11", "text": "Y Dios dijo: \"Produzca la tierra hierba, hierbas semillando semilla, árboles frutales haciendo fruto según su especie, cuya semilla <em>esta</em> en el, sobre la tierra.\" Y fue así.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>VERBO RARO - \"PRODUCIR HIERBA\"</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>תַּדְשֵׁא</strong> (<em>tadsheh</em>) = verbo creado del sustantivo <strong>דֶּשֶׁא</strong> (hierba)--similar a \"enherbar.\" SI, suena extraño--<strong>preservacíon intenciónal del estilo poético hebreo.</strong></li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>PATRONES DE DUPLICACION DE RAIZ</strong> (Recurso poético hebreo)", "body": "<ul><li><strong>מַזְרִיעַ זֶרַע</strong> (<em>mazria zera</em>) = \"semillando semilla\"; <strong>עֹשֶׂה פְרִי</strong> (<em>oseh pri</em>) = \"haciendo fruto\"</li><li>Muestra producción/generación interna--<strong>preservado a pesar de sonar forzado</strong></li><li><strong>דֶּשֶׁא עֵשֶׂב</strong> (<em>deshe esev</em>) = \"hierba, hierbas\" (par de sinonimos por efecto estilístico)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>PATRON DE REPRODUCCION</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>לְמִינוֹ</strong> (<em>lemino</em>) = \"según su especie/tipo\"--describe patron de reproducción</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "12", "text": "Y la tierra produjo hierba, hierbas semillando semilla según su especie, y árboles haciendo fruto cuya semilla <em>esta</em> en el, según su especie. Y Dios vio que bueno.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>PATRON MANDATO - CUMPLIMIENTO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>v.11 mandato - v.12 cumplimiento con redacción casí idéntica--muestra cumplimiento exacto</li><li>Duplicación de raíz mantenida: \"semillando semilla,\" \"haciendo fruto\"</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "13", "text": "Y fue tarde, y fue mañana, tercer día.", "notes": []}, {"n": "14", "text": "Y Dios dijo: \"Haya luminares en el raqia, para separar entre el día y entre la noche, y sean para señales y para tiempos determinados y para días y años.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>LUMINARES INTRODUCIDOS</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>מְאֹרֹת</strong> (<em>me'orot</em>) = luces/luminares/portadores de luz de la raíz <strong>א-ו-ר</strong> (luz)--plural pero referentes específicos no nombrados hasta v.16</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>REFERENCIA AL RAQIA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Tras la identificación del v.8 raqia = cielo, este versículo coloca luminares \"en el raqia\"</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>TIEMPOS DETERMINADOS</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>מוֹעֲדִים</strong> (<em>mo'adim</em>) = tiempos determinados/estaciónes/festividades--puede significar estaciónes naturales O eventos del calendario sagrado; rango de significado preservado</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "15", "text": "Y sean para luminares en el raqia, para alumbrar sobre la tierra.\" Y fue así.", "notes": []}, {"n": "16", "text": "Y Dios hizo los dos grandes luminares: el luminar mayor para dominio del día, y el luminar menor para dominio de la noche, y las estrellas.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - LUMINARES SIN NOMBRE</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Sol y luna <strong>DEJADOS SIN NOMBRE</strong>--descritos solo como \"luminar mayor\" y \"luminar menor\"</li><li>Contexto del antiguo Cercano Oriente: evitando nombres de deidades usados en culturas circundantes</li><li>La Edición Transparente resiste identificarlos por nombre</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>DOMINIO = GOBIERNO TEMPORAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>מֶמְשֶׁלֶת</strong> (<em>memsheleth</em>) = dominio/gobierno sobre <strong>períodos de tiempo</strong>--NO gobierno territorial</li><li>\"Y las estrellas\" anadido casí como nota al margen sintactica--la estructura enfatiza las dos luces</li><li><strong>עָשָׂה</strong> (<em>asah</em> = hizo) usado, NO <strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = creo)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "17", "text": "Y Dios los puso en el raqia, para alumbrar sobre la tierra.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>COLOCACION</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Luminares puestos <strong>EN</strong> el raqia--contraste: aves vuelan <strong>SOBRE</strong> el raqia (v.20)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "18", "text": "Y para gobernar en el día y en la noche, y para separar entre la luz y entre las tinieblas. Y Dios vio que bueno.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>INFINITIVOS DE PROPOSITO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>\"Para gobernar...y para separar\"--funciónes paralelas de los luminares</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "19", "text": "Y fue tarde, y fue mañana, cuarto día.", "notes": []}, {"n": "20", "text": "Y Dios dijo: \"Pululen las aguas <em>de</em> enjambres de seres vivos, y aves vuelen sobre la tierra, sobre la faz del raqia.\"", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - SERES VIVOS INTRODUCIDOS</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה</strong> (<em>nefesh chayah</em>) = ser(es) vivo(s)--literalmente \"aliento/garganta/alma viviente\"; <strong>NO \"alma\" en el sentido filosófico posterior</strong></li><li>Anadido al glosario; usado en vv.21, 24, 30</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>DUPLICACION DE RAIZ</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>שֶׁרֶץ</strong> (<em>sherets</em> = enjambres) de <strong>יִשְׁרְצוּ</strong> (<em>yishretzu</em> = pululen)</li><li><strong>יְעוֹפֵף</strong> (<em>ye'ofef</em>) = forma duplicada/intensiva \"volando-volar\"</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>RELACION ESPACIAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Las aves vuelan <strong>SOBRE la faz del</strong> raqia--NO <strong>EN</strong> el (contraste: luminares <strong>EN</strong> el raqia)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "21", "text": "Y Dios creó las grandes criaturas marinas, y todo ser vivo, los que se mueven que las aguas pulularon, según sus especies, y toda ave alada según su especie. Y Dios vio que bueno.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - CREO, NO HIZO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = creo) regresa por primera vez desde v.1--usado para seres vivos, NO para luminares o plantas; sugiere distinción de significado</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>CRIATURAS MARINAS</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>תַּנִּינִים</strong> (<em>taninim</em>) = grandes criaturas marinas/grandes animales acuaticos--evitar \"monstruos marinos\" o \"dragones\" (superposición mitológica)</li><li><strong>לְמִינֵהֶם/לְמִינֵהוּ</strong> (<em>leminehem/leminehu</em>) = \"según sus especies\"--patron de reproducción como en v.11</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "22", "text": "Y Dios los bendijo, diciendo: \"Sean fecundos y multiplíquense, y llenen las aguas en los mares, y <em>que</em> se multipliquen las aves en la tierra.\"", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>PRIMERA FORMULA DE BENDICION</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>וַיְבָרֶךְ</strong> (<em>vayvarekh</em>) = \"y los bendijo\" (primera ocurrencia)--recurrira: v.28 (humanos), Génesis 2:3 (septimo día)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>TRIPLE IMPERATIVO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>פְּרוּ</strong> (<em>peru</em>) = sean fecundos; <strong>וּרְבוּ</strong> (<em>urvu</em>) = multiplíquense; <strong>וּמִלְאוּ</strong> (<em>umil'u</em>) = llenen</li><li><strong>לֵאמֹר</strong> (<em>lemor</em> = \"diciendo\") introduce discurso divino directo a las criaturas--característica narrativa inusual</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "23", "text": "Y fue tarde, y fue mañana, quinto día.", "notes": []}, {"n": "24", "text": "Y Dios dijo: \"Produzca la tierra seres vivos según su especie: ganado y cosas que se arrastran y animales de <em>la</em> tierra, según su especie.\" Y fue así.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>NEFESH CHAYAH - Animales Terrestres</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה</strong> ahora aplicado a animales terrestres (previamente criaturas acuaticas, vv.20-21)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>TRES CATEGORIAS</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בְּהֵמָה</strong> (<em>behemah</em>) = ganado; <strong>רֶמֶשׂ</strong> (<em>remes</em>) = lo que se arrastra; <strong>חַיְתוֹ־אֶרֶץ</strong> (<em>chayeto-eretz</em>) = animales de la tierra/animales salvajes</li><li>El patron es paralelo a la vegetación del Día 3: la tierra produce por mandato divino</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "25", "text": "Y Dios hizo los animales de la tierra según su especie, y el ganado según su especie, y todo lo que se arrastra del suelo según su especie. Y Dios vio que bueno.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>SUELO vs. TIERRA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>אֲדָמָה</strong> (<em>adamah</em>) = suelo (PRIMERA ocurrencia)--distinto de <strong>אֶרֶץ</strong> (<em>eretz</em> = tierra)</li><li><strong>עָשָׂה</strong> (<em>asah</em> = hizo), NO <strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = creo)</li><li>Mandato (v.24) - cumplimiento (v.25) como en los Días 3-4</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "26", "text": "Y Dios dijo: \"Hagamos <em>un</em> humano a nuestra imagen, conforme a nuestra semejanza, y dominen sobre <em>los</em> peces del mar y sobre <em>las</em> aves del cielo y sobre el ganado y sobre toda la tierra y sobre todo lo que se arrastra <em>que</em> se arrastra sobre la tierra.\"", "notes": [{"type": "theological", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - DISCURSO DIVINO PLURAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Primera persona <strong>PLURAL</strong>: \"hagamos...a nuestra imagen...nuestra semejanza\"</li><li>Interpretaciones <strong>POSIBLES</strong>: (1) plural mayestatico, (2) consejo divino, (3) plural literario</li><li>La nota marca <strong>INCERTIDUMBRE</strong>--NO impone interpretación trinitaria</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>HUMANO = GENERICO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>אָדָם</strong> (<em>adam</em>) SIN artículo = humano/humanidad genérica--NO todavía nombre propio \"Adan\"</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>IMAGEN Y SEMEJANZA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>צֶלֶם</strong> (<em>tselem</em>) = imagen; <strong>דְּמוּת</strong> (<em>demut</em>) = semejanza</li><li>Ambos = representación/parecido; emparejados para enfasis, NO significado idéntico</li><li><strong>Referencia cruzada:</strong> El par reaparece en <strong>Gen 5:1-3</strong> donde Adan engendra a Set <em>\"a su semejanza, conforme a su imagen\"</em> — invirtiendo el orden divino-humano a un descenso humano-humano y encadenando el lenguaje de creación a través de las generaciónes.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>DOMINIO = GOBIERNO FUNCIONAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>רָדָה</strong> (<em>radah</em>) = dominar/gobernar--autoridad funciónal, <strong>NO propiedad</strong></li><li>Cambio de verbo: \"hagamos UN humano\" (singular) - \"dominen\" (plural)</li><li><strong>הָרֶמֶשׂ הָֽרֹמֵשׂ</strong> (<em>haremes haromes</em>) = \"lo que se arrastra que se arrastra\" (duplicación de raiz)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "27", "text": "Y Dios creó al humano a su imagen; a <em>la</em> imagen de Dios lo creó; varón y hembra los creó.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - TRIPLE ENFASIS DE CREACION</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>בָּרָא</strong> (<em>bara</em> = creo) usado <strong>TRES VECES</strong>--<strong>UNICA ocurrencia</strong> de triple repetición verbal en un versículo; muestra maxima significación/enfasis</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>ESTRUCTURA POETICA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Tres clausulas paralelas con <strong>bara</strong> anclando cada una--estilo literario elevado</li><li>Cambio singular/plural: \"el humano...lo\" (SINGULAR) - \"varón y hembra...los\" (PLURAL)--la humanidad colectiva se diferencia</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>DIFERENCIACION BIOLOGICA</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>זָכָר וּנְקֵבָה</strong> (<em>zakhar unqevah</em>) = varón y hembra--términos gramaticales para sexo biologico, NO roles culturales de genero</li><li><strong>הָאָדָם</strong> (<em>ha'adam</em>) = \"EL humano\" (con artículo) vs. v.26 <strong>אָדָם</strong> (sin artículo)--<strong>POSIBLE</strong> enfasis</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "28", "text": "Y Dios los bendijo, y Dios les dijo: \"Sean fecundos y multiplíquense, y llenen la tierra y sojúzguenla, y dominen sobre <em>los</em> peces del mar y sobre <em>las</em> aves del cielo y sobre todo ser vivo <em>que</em> se mueve sobre la tierra.\"", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>FORMULA DE BENDICION</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Como v.22 (criaturas marinas/aves), pero expandida para humaños con mandatos adicionales</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CINCO IMPERATIVOS</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Sean fecundos, multiplíquense, llenen, <strong>sojúzguenla</strong>, <strong>dominen</strong></li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>SOJUZGAR = CULTIVO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>כָּבַשׁ</strong> (<em>kabash</em>) = sojuzgar/poner bajo cultivo--término agricola (aparece SOLO aquí en Génesis 1); <strong>NO licencia para explotación o violencia</strong></li><li><strong>רָדָה</strong> (<em>radah</em>) ahora como imperativo--gobierno funciónal sobre animales, NO propiedad absoluta</li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>REFERENCIA CRUZADA: REPETICION POST-DILUVIO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>El mandato \"sean fecundos y multiplíquense y llenen la tierra\" reaparece textualmente en <strong>Gen 9:1</strong> tras el diluvio — mismo mandato estructural, pero el lenguaje de dominio cambia de tono (Gen 9:2–3). Para una discusión más completa, vea el compañero Sección D.</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "29", "text": "Y Dios dijo: \"He aquí, les he dado toda hierba semillando semilla que <em>esta</em> sobre <em>la</em> faz de toda la tierra, y todo árbol en el cual <em>hay</em> fruto de <em>un</em> árbol semillando semilla; a ustedes será para alimento.", "notes": [{"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>PARTICULA DE ATENCION</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>הִנֵּה</strong> (<em>hineh</em>) = \"he aquí\"--senala anuncio importante</li></ul>"}, {"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>DUPLICACION DE RAIZ</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>זֹרֵעַ זֶרַע</strong> (<em>zorea zera</em>) = \"semillando semilla\"--patron de vv.11-12</li></ul>"}, {"type": "theological", "title": "<strong>DIETA ORIGINAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>Vegetación UNICAMENTE para humanos--NO se permite consumo animal aun (contraste Génesis 9:3 permiso post-diluvio)</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "30", "text": "Y a todo ser vivo de la tierra y a toda ave del cielo y a todo lo que se arrastra sobre la tierra, en el cual <em>hay</em> ser vivo, toda hierba verde <em>será</em> para alimento.\" Y fue así.", "notes": [{"type": "lexical", "title": "<strong>NEFESH CHAYAH = Calificador</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה</strong> distingue animales con aliento/vida de las plantas</li></ul>"}, {"type": "theological", "title": "<strong>DIETA VEGETARIANA UNIVERSAL</strong>", "body": "<ul><li>TODOS los seres vivos comen solo plantas inicialmente--los animales también vegetariaños en la creación original</li><li><strong>יֶרֶק עֵשֶׂב</strong> (<em>yereq esev</em>) = hierba verde/vegetación fresca</li></ul>"}]}, {"n": "31", "text": "Y Dios vio todo lo que había hecho, y he aquí, <em>era</em> muy bueno. Y fue tarde, y fue mañana, el sexto día.", "notes": [{"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - CAMBIO DE EVALUACION: MUY BUENO</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>טוֹב מְאֹד</strong> (<em>tov me'od</em>) = \"MUY bueno\" vs. simple <strong>טוֹב</strong> (<em>tov</em> = \"bueno\") en TODOS los días anteriores</li><li><strong>UNICA ocurrencia</strong> de \"muy bueno\" en el relato de la creación--muestra evaluación positiva integral tras la creación humana</li><li><strong>ESTO NO ES VARIACION ESTILISTICA--ES SIGNIFICACION TEOLÓGICA</strong></li></ul>"}, {"type": "grammatical", "title": "<strong>HINEH = Atencion</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>הִנֵּה</strong> (<em>hineh</em> = \"he aquí\") aparece con la evaluación--llama la atención sobre la bondad integral</li><li>\"Todo lo que había hecho\"--toda la creación revisada</li></ul>"}, {"type": "critical", "title": "<strong>CRÍTICO - ARTICULO EN \"EL SEXTO DIA\"</strong>", "body": "<ul><li><strong>יוֹם הַשִּׁשִּׁי</strong> (<em>yom hashishi</em>) = \"EL sexto día\" con artículo definido <strong>ה</strong></li><li><strong>UNICO entre los seis días</strong> (Días 1-5 NO tienen artículo)</li><li><strong>POSIBLE</strong> significado: enfasis de culminación, importancia de la creación humana, o preparación para el Sabado (Génesis 2:1-3)</li><li><strong>Muchas traducciónes omiten esta distinción</strong></li></ul>"}]}], "glossary": {"headers": ["Hebreo", "Español", "Notas"], "rows": [["אֱלֹהִים", "Dios", "Forma plural, verbo singular"], ["אֶרֶץ", "tierra", "\"Suelo\" solo cuando claramente se refiere al suelo"], ["אֲדָמָה", "suelo", "Distinto de <em>eretz</em>"], ["שָׁמַיִם", "cielo, cielos", "NO \"Cielo\" espíritual"], ["רָקִיעַ", "raqia", "Transliterado; v.8 = cielo"], ["מַיִם", "aguas <em>(por defecto)</em> / agua <em>(contextual)</em>", "Plural por defecto donde el contexto es plural-significativo (cuerpos separados, aguas reunidas). Singular contextual \"agua\" permitido donde forzar \"aguas\" importaria registro de Reina-Valera; evaluar según Regla 3. Todos los cambios registrados."], ["רוּחַ", "viento/espíritu", "Puede agregar \"aliento\" en notas. Fem. en hebreo; masc. en español."], ["תְהוֹם", "el abismo", "Evitar especulación. Fem. en hebreo; masc. en español."], ["תֹהוּ וָבֹהוּ", "caos y vacío", "Raro; significado incierto"], ["נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה", "ser(es) vivo(s)", "NO \"alma\" filosoficamente"], ["בָּרָא", "creó", "Creación divina; v.1, 21, 27"], ["עָשָׂה", "hizo", "Formación; v.7, 16, 25"], ["צֶלֶם", "imagen", "Emparejado con <em>demut</em>"], ["דְּמוּת", "semejanza", "Emparejado con <em>tselem</em>"], ["אָדָם", "humano", "Generico; \"Adan\" cuando es nombre propio"], ["רָדָה", "dominar", "Gobierno funciónal"], ["כָּבַשׁ", "sojuzgar", "Termino agricola"]]}, "supplementary": [{"title": "SEGUIMIENTO DE FORMULAS", "body": "<p><strong>Formulas Fijas (Ocurrencias Multiples):</strong></p><ul><li>\"Y Dios dijo...\" (10x)</li><li>\"Y fue así\" (6x — vv.7, 9, 11, 15, 24, 30)</li><li>\"Y Dios vio que bueno\" (6x) + \"muy bueno\" (1x en v.31)</li><li>\"Y fue tarde, y fue mañana, [X] día\" (6x)</li><li>\"Y Dios los bendijo\" (2x: vv.22, 28)</li><li>\"Sean fecundos y multiplíquense\" (2x: vv.22, 28)</li></ul><p><strong>Variaciones Significativas:</strong></p><ul><li>v.5: \"día uno\" (cardinal) vs. vv.8,13,19,23,31 (ordinales)</li><li>v.31: \"muy bueno\" (NO simple \"bueno\") + \"EL sexto día\" (artículo único)</li></ul>"}, {"title": "PATRONES DE DUPLICACION DE RAIZ", "body": "<p>Recurso poético hebreo que muestra generación interna:</p><ul><li>v.11-12: \"semillando semilla\" (<strong>מַזְרִיעַ זֶרַע</strong>), \"haciendo fruto\" (<strong>עֹשֶׂה פְרִי</strong>)</li><li>v.20: \"enjambres\" de \"pululen\"</li><li>v.26: \"lo que se arrastra que se arrastra\" (<strong>הָרֶמֶשׂ הָֽרֹמֵשׂ</strong>)</li><li>v.29: \"semillando semilla\" (<strong>זֹרֵעַ זֶרַע</strong>)</li></ul><p><strong>Preservado a pesar de sonar forzado--estilo poético hebreo intenciónal.</strong></p>"}, {"title": "CAMBIOS DE VERBO - CREO vs. HIZO", "body": "<table class=\"cmp\"><thead><tr><th>Versículo</th><th>Acción</th><th>Verbo</th><th>Hebreo</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>v.1</td><td>Cielos y tierra</td><td><strong>creo</strong></td><td><em>bara</em> בָּרָא</td></tr><tr><td>v.7</td><td>Raqia</td><td>hizo</td><td><em>asah</em> עָשָׂה</td></tr><tr><td>v.16</td><td>Luminares</td><td>hizo</td><td><em>asah</em></td></tr><tr><td>v.21</td><td>Criaturas marinas y seres vivos</td><td><strong>creo</strong></td><td><em>bara</em></td></tr><tr><td>v.25</td><td>Animales terrestres</td><td>hizo</td><td><em>asah</em></td></tr><tr><td>v.27</td><td>Humano (3x enfasis)</td><td><strong>creo</strong></td><td><em>bara</em></td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Patron:</strong> <em>Bara</em> (creo) para creación inicial, seres vivos, humanos. <em>Asah</em> (hizo) para raqia, luminares, animales terrestres. <strong>POSIBLE</strong> distinción: <em>bara</em> se usa distintivamente para la acción creativa divina; su alcance preciso (si implica creación de la nada o remodelación de material existente) es debatido.</p><p><strong>FIN DE GÉNESIS 1 - LA TRADUCCIÓN TRANSPARENTE (ESPAÑOL)</strong></p>"}]}};
